    ("The Simurgh and the Huma Bird (Mantiq al-Tayr)", "Habiballah of Sava", 1600, "Opaque watercolor and gold on paper", "Safavid Persian / Islamic", ["illuminated manuscript","colorful","decorative","symbolic","narrative"], ["mythical birds","simurgh","landscape","Persian poetry"], ["gold","blue","green","red","cream"], "Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York", "A magnificent double-page spread from the Conference of the Birds showing mythical birds in a paradise landscape.", "One of the finest surviving Safavid manuscripts. The poem by Attar is a Sufi allegory; the paintings achieve a dazzling harmony of text and image.", "male", "Persian"),
    ("Layla and Majnun at School (Khamsa of Nizami)", "Bihzad", 1494, "Opaque watercolor and gold", "Timurid Persian / Islamic", ["miniature","detailed","architectural","narrative","refined"], ["school","children","teacher","Layla","Majnun","love"], ["blue","gold","red","green","cream"], "British Library, London", "The young lovers Layla and Majnun meet as children in a colorful madrasa school depicted with precise architectural detail.", "Bihzad is considered the greatest Persian miniature painter. The composition's perspective and human observation are without peer in his era.", "male", "Persian"),
    ("Bahram Gur Hunting (Khamsa of Nizami)", "Sultan Muhammad", 1539, "Opaque watercolor and gold", "Safavid Persian / Islamic", ["miniature","royal hunt","colorful","dynamic","Safavid"], ["king","hunting","horses","deer","landscape"], ["gold","blue","red","green"], "British Library, London", "The legendary Persian king Bahram Gur hunts onagers from horseback with his slave girl Azada playing a harp.", "Sultan Muhammad's masterpiece. The swirling energy, impossible gold horizon, and packed detail define the Safavid Tabriz school.", "male", "Persian"),
    ("The Miraj (Night Journey of the Prophet)", "Unknown Safavid artist", 1539, "Opaque watercolor and gold", "Safavid Persian / Islamic", ["religious","celestial","colorful","symbolic","divine"], ["Prophet Muhammad","Buraq","angels","fire","ascension"], ["gold","blue","red","flame orange","cream"], "Bibliothèque nationale de France, Paris", "The Prophet Muhammad rides the celestial steed Buraq through a sky filled with angels during his Night Journey to heaven.", "One of the most celebrated images of Islamic art. The golden nimbus and flame angels merge Persian aesthetic with Islamic theology.", "unknown", "Persian"),
    ("Rustam Slays the Dragon (Shahnameh)", "Unknown Safavid artist", 1560, "Opaque watercolor and gold on paper", "Safavid Persian / Islamic", ["epic","heroic","colorful","narrative","illuminated"], ["hero","dragon","battle","landscape","epic"], ["red","gold","green","blue","dramatic"], "Various collections", "The hero Rustam drives his lance into the dragon's mouth while his horse Rakhsh attacks the creature from behind.", "From the illustrated Shahnameh (Book of Kings), Iran's national epic. The finest Shahnameh manuscripts are among the greatest books ever made.", "unknown", "Persian"),
    ("Blue Quran Page", "Unknown Fatimid artists", 900, "Gold kufic on parchment dyed with indigo", "Abbasid / Fatimid / Islamic", ["calligraphy","gold","geometric","devotional","manuscript"], ["Quranic verse","gold lettering","indigo page","arabic script"], ["deep blue","gold"], "Various collections worldwide", "A full page of the Quran written in gold kufic script on parchment dyed indigo blue — among the most precious manuscripts ever made.", "The Blue Quran is believed to have been made for the Great Mosque of Kairouan. Its gold-on-blue combination is unique in Islamic manuscript history.", "unknown", "North African"),
    ("Mosaic of the Great Mosque of Damascus", "Byzantine and Arab craftsmen", 715, "Glass mosaic", "Umayyad / Islamic", ["architectural","mosaic","decorative","paradise","panoramic"], ["paradise garden","trees","architecture","river","nature"], ["gold","green","blue","white","Byzantine tesserae"], "Umayyad Mosque, Damascus", "The mosaic frieze in the courtyard of the Great Mosque depicts a paradise of lush trees, rivers, and fantastical architecture with no human figures.", "The largest extant early Islamic mosaic in the world. Combines Byzantine technique with Islamic iconoclasm — landscape paradise without figures.", "unknown", "Syrian"),

    # ── AFRICAN ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    ("Benin Bronze: Queen Mother Idia Pendant Mask", "Benin Court artists", 1500, "Ivory and iron", "Benin Kingdom / West African", ["court art","refined","symbolic","royal","portrait"], ["queen mother","portrait","royalty","beaded collar","iron pupils"], ["ivory white","iron dark"], "British Museum, London", "An exquisite ivory pendant mask depicting Queen Mother Idia with iron-inlaid pupils and a tiara of miniature Portuguese heads.", "One of the finest works of African court art. The icon of the FESTAC symbol. Looted in the 1897 British Punitive Expedition.", "unknown", "Nigerian"),
    ("Benin Bronze Plaque: Oba with Attendants", "Benin Court bronzesmiths", 1550, "Cast bronze", "Benin Kingdom / West African", ["court art","bronze","hierarchical","narrative","military"], ["Oba","attendants","warriors","hierarchical scale","court"], ["bronze brown","patina green"], "Ethnologisches Museum, Berlin", "A cast bronze plaque showing the Oba (king) flanked by warriors and attendants in hierarchical scale, with flowing decorative detail.", "The Benin Bronzes — over 4000 works looted by Britain in 1897 — are among the most technically advanced bronzes made anywhere in the world.", "unknown", "Nigerian"),
    ("Ife Bronze Head", "Ife Court artists", 1200, "Cast bronze", "Ife Kingdom / Yoruba", ["court art","naturalistic","bronze","portrait","serene"], ["royal head","portrait","naturalistic face","ceremonial"], ["bronze warm","patina"], "Ife Museum, Nigeria", "A near-photorealistic bronze head of an Ife king or deity, with delicate parallel scarification lines and a dignified expression.", "The Ife bronzes shocked Western art historians who doubted African artists could achieve such naturalism. Now recognized as a world summit of portraiture.", "unknown", "Nigerian"),
    ("Kuba Ndop (Royal Portrait) of King Shamba Bolongongo", "Kuba artists", 1620, "Carved wood", "Kuba Kingdom / Central African", ["court portrait","carved","symbolic","throne","ceremonial"], ["king","seated figure","ndop","emblems","royal"], ["dark wood brown"], "Brooklyn Museum", "A carved wooden seated figure of the Kuba king with a weaving board (representing his invention of raffia cloth weaving) as his personal emblem.", "The oldest surviving Kuba ndop sculpture. Each Kuba king's ndop was believed to house his spirit. A masterwork of African portrait sculpture.", "unknown", "Congolese"),
    ("Dogon Seated Couple", "Dogon sculptors", 1700, "Carved wood", "Dogon / West African", ["sculptural","paired","symbolic","spiritual","elongated"], ["seated couple","male female","creation","ancestors","primordial"], ["dark wood","worn patina"], "Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York", "Two elongated seated figures — male and female — rigidly posed and joined, representing the first human couple in Dogon cosmology.", "A canonical work of African sculpture and a cornerstone of any world art survey. The figures represent the cosmic order of paired opposites.", "unknown", "Malian"),
    ("Luba Kifwebe Mask", "Luba-Hemba artists", 1800, "Carved and painted wood", "Luba / Central African", ["mask","geometric","striped","spiritual","ceremonial"], ["mask","stripes","geometric","power","spirit"], ["white","brown","red stripes"], "Various collections", "A mask with bold parallel incised grooves over its surface, used in initiation and governance ceremonies.", "Luba kifwebe masks are among the most powerful formal achievements in African art. Their geometric rigor influenced Cubism.", "unknown", "Congolese"),
    ("Great Zimbabwe Bird Soapstone Stelae", "Zimbabwe stone carvers", 1300, "Carved soapstone", "Great Zimbabwe / Shona", ["monumental","symbolic","carved","architectural","bird"], ["bird","soapstone","pillar","eagle","throne"], ["grey soapstone"], "Great Zimbabwe Monument", "A carved soapstone bird atop a pillar, originally sited on the massive dry-stone walls of Great Zimbabwe.", "The Zimbabwe Bird is the national symbol of Zimbabwe. Eight were found at Great Zimbabwe and scattered by colonial looting. Symbol of pre-colonial civilization.", "unknown", "Zimbabwean"),

    # ── PRE-COLUMBIAN & MESOAMERICAN ───────────────────────────────────────
    ("Aztec Calendar Stone (Sun Stone)", "Mexica sculptors", 1479, "Carved basalt", "Aztec / Mesoamerican", ["monumental","symbolic","cosmic","carved","religious"], ["sun","calendar","cosmic","Aztec","gods","time"], ["grey basalt"], "National Museum of Anthropology, Mexico City", "A 24-ton basalt disc carved with the Aztec solar calendar, the sun god Tonatiuh at center, surrounded by cosmic ages and day signs.", "The most iconic object of Mesoamerican civilization. Misnamed a 'calendar', it is actually a cosmological monument celebrating the Fifth Sun.", "unknown", "Aztec"),
    ("Olmec Colossal Head No. 1", "Olmec sculptors", -900, "Carved basalt", "Olmec / Mesoamerican", ["monumental","portrait","massive","carved","ancient"], ["head","portrait","helmet","ruler","massive boulder"], ["dark basalt"], "Museo de Antropología, Jalapa", "A colossal basalt head of an Olmec ruler, nearly 3 meters tall, with individualized features and a distinctive helmet.", "The Olmec Colossal Heads are among the most astonishing sculptural achievements of the ancient world. Each depicts an individual ruler.", "unknown", "Mexican"),
    ("Mayan Bonampak Murals (Room 1)", "Maya court painters", 790, "Mineral pigment on plaster", "Classic Maya / Mesoamerican", ["mural","colorful","narrative","court","ritual"], ["court ceremony","musicians","procession","nobles","ritual"], ["blue","red","green","ochre","cream"], "Bonampak archaeological site, Chiapas", "Room 1 murals show a Maya court ceremony: nobles in jade jewelry, musicians with instruments, and a child being presented.", "The most complete surviving Maya murals. Only discovered in 1946, they revolutionized understanding of Maya art and warfare rituals.", "unknown", "Mayan"),
    ("Nazca Lines: Hummingbird", "Nazca culture", -200, "Earth geoglyph", "Nazca / Andean", ["geoglyph","monumental","aerial","symbolic","geometric"], ["hummingbird","earth lines","desert","symbolic"], ["desert brown","pale earth"], "Nazca Desert, Peru", "A single continuous line etched into the desert floor forming a giant hummingbird with stylized beak and wing feathers.", "Among 70 zoomorphic geoglyphs only visible from the air. Still debated for purpose — ritual, astronomical, or directional.", "unknown", "Peruvian"),
    ("Wari Tunic", "Wari weavers", 700, "Tapestry weave wool and cotton", "Wari / Andean", ["textile","geometric","colorful","abstract","symbolic"], ["geometric pattern","tunic","abstract faces","stepped","colorful"], ["red","blue","gold","white","black"], "Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York", "A tapestry-woven tunic covered in interlocking stepped patterns that break down into abstract faces when examined closely.", "Wari textiles are among the most technically complex fabrics ever produced. The hidden face imagery reflects Andean belief systems.", "unknown", "Peruvian"),

    # ── GRECO-ROMAN & ANCIENT MEDITERRANEAN ───────────────────────────────
    ("Laocoön and His Sons", "Agesander, Athenodoros, Polydoros of Rhodes", -40, "Marble sculpture group", "Hellenistic / Greek", ["dramatic","agony","twisting","classical","sculptural"], ["Laocoön","sons","serpents","agony","myth"], ["white marble"], "Vatican Museums, Rome", "The Trojan priest Laocoön and his two sons writhe in agony as sea serpents crush them, captured in white marble.", "Rediscovered in 1506 and profoundly influenced Michelangelo and the entire Renaissance. Exemplifies Hellenistic pathos and the 'figura serpentinata'.", "male", "Greek"),
    ("Discobolus (Discus Thrower)", "Myron (Roman copy)", -450, "Marble (Roman copy of bronze original)", "Classical Greek", ["athletic","ideal","dynamic","classical","sculptural"], ["athlete","discus","throwing","ideal body","youth"], ["white marble"], "Museo Nazionale Romano, Rome", "An athlete at the moment of maximum tension before releasing the discus, his body twisted into a perfect arc.", "The original was bronze, now lost. Roman copies preserve what was considered the ideal of male athletic beauty in classical Greece.", "male", "Greek"),
    ("Nike of Samothrace (Winged Victory)", "Unknown Greek sculptor", -190, "Marble sculpture", "Hellenistic / Greek", ["dramatic","wind-swept","dynamic","monumental","sculptural"], ["Nike","wings","wind","prow of ship","victory"], ["white marble"], "Louvre Museum, Paris", "The goddess of victory alights on the prow of a ship, her drapery blown back by sea wind, her wings spread wide.", "Among the greatest surviving Greek sculptures. The wind-blown drapery reveals the body beneath with extraordinary skill. Found in 1863.", "unknown", "Greek"),
    ("Fayum Mummy Portrait", "Unknown Greco-Egyptian artists", 200, "Encaustic on wood panel", "Roman Egypt / Greco-Roman", ["portrait","realistic","individual","intimate","encaustic"], ["portrait","eyes","face","mummy","individual"], ["warm skin tone","dark eyes","cream","gold"], "Various museums worldwide", "An individual portrait painted in encaustic wax on a wood panel, attached to the mummy of its subject after death.", "The Fayum portraits are the most realistic ancient portraits that survive. They preserve individual faces from Roman Egypt with startling immediacy.", "unknown", "Egyptian"),
    ("Stele of Hammurabi", "Babylonian sculptors", -1754, "Carved diorite", "Babylonian / Mesopotamian", ["monumental","legal","symbolic","narrative","carved"], ["king","sun god","law code","cuneiform","ceremony"], ["black diorite"], "Louvre Museum, Paris", "A black stone stele showing the sun god Shamash granting the law code to King Hammurabi, followed by 282 cuneiform laws.", "One of the oldest surviving legal documents. The relief at the top is a masterpiece of Babylonian court art.", "unknown", "Iraqi"),
    ("Bust of Nefertiti", "Thutmose (attr.)", -1345, "Painted limestone", "New Kingdom Egypt / Ancient", ["portrait","regal","refined","painted","iconic"], ["queen","crown","portrait","elegant","beauty"], ["blue crown","gold","painted skin","cream"], "Neues Museum, Berlin", "Queen Nefertiti's bust with the iconic blue flat-top crown and aristocratic painted face, one eye unfinished.", "One of the most copied works of ancient art. The elegant proportions and refined colour represent the peak of Amarna period aesthetics.", "unknown", "Egyptian"),
    ("The Standard of Ur", "Sumerian craftsmen", -2600, "Shell, lapis lazuli, red limestone on wood", "Sumerian / Mesopotamian", ["narrative","mosaic","ancient","symbolic","register"], ["war","peace","soldiers","chariots","banquet","procession"], ["blue lapis","white shell","red limestone"], "British Museum, London", "Two registers — 'War' and 'Peace' — depict Sumerian military victory and royal banquet in inlaid mosaic panels.", "One of the oldest narrative artworks. The inlaid registers showing war and celebration give unique insight into Sumerian society.", "unknown", "Iraqi"),
    ("Seated Scribe", "Unknown Egyptian sculptor", -2620, "Painted limestone", "Old Kingdom Egypt / Ancient", ["portrait","realistic","seated","painted","ancient"], ["scribe","seated cross-legged","scroll","attentive","individual"], ["painted skin","white kilt","dark eyes"], "Louvre Museum, Paris", "A lifelike painted limestone scribe sits cross-legged with a papyrus scroll on his lap and an intensely alert gaze.", "The realistic painted eyes (rock crystal, copper, white magnesite) create an unnerving sense of life. One of the peaks of Old Kingdom sculpture.", "unknown", "Egyptian"),

    # ── BYZANTINE & MEDIEVAL EUROPE ───────────────────────────────────────
    ("Pantocrator Mosaic, Cefalu Cathedral", "Byzantine mosaicists", 1148, "Glass tesserae mosaic", "Byzantine / Medieval", ["mosaic","gold","religious","frontal","hieratic"], ["Christ","Pantocrator","gold background","blessing","Byzantine"], ["gold","blue","red","cream","white"], "Cefalù Cathedral, Sicily", "Christ as Pantocrator (Ruler of All) gazes from the apse in golden mosaic, right hand blessing, left holding the Gospels.", "The finest Pantocrator mosaic outside Istanbul. Norman king Roger II commissioned it. The hierarchical scale and gold background define Byzantine aesthetic.", "unknown", "Byzantine"),
    ("Book of Kells: Chi-Rho Page", "Irish monks (Iona/Kells)", 800, "Ink and pigment on vellum", "Insular / Celtic", ["illuminated manuscript","intricate","symbolic","geometric","celtic"], ["chi-rho","interlace","animals","spirals","Christian symbol"], ["gold","red","blue","green","cream"], "Trinity College Library, Dublin", "The Chi-Rho page — the monogram of Christ — is elaborated into a dense web of interlace, spirals, and hidden animals.", "The most celebrated page in Western manuscript art. The density of decoration required months of work under a magnifying glass.", "unknown", "Irish"),
    ("Bayeux Tapestry (Comet Scene)", "Norman or Anglo-Saxon embroiderers", 1077, "Embroidery on linen", "Romanesque / Medieval", ["narrative","sequential","linear","historical","embroidery"], ["Halley's Comet","crowd","portent","battle","Harold","ships"], ["wool thread","linen","narrative registers"], "Bayeux Tapestry Museum, Normandy", "The comet scene shows Halley's Comet blazing overhead while Harold's frightened counselors point upward — a portent of doom.", "A 70-meter embroidered cartoon of the Norman Conquest. Unique survival of medieval narrative textile art.", "unknown", "French/English"),
    ("Limbourg Brothers: Les Très Riches Heures (October)", "Pol, Herman, Jean de Limbourg", 1412, "Tempera and gold on vellum", "International Gothic / Flemish", ["illuminated manuscript","seasonal","detailed","gothic","gold"], ["harvest","peasants","fields","castle","October"], ["blue","gold","brown","green","cream"], "Musée Condé, Chantilly", "Peasants sowing fields before the Louvre palace in October light, with a falconer and dog in the foreground.", "The greatest illuminated manuscript of the International Gothic style. The Limbourg brothers died of plague before completion.", "male", "Dutch"),
    ("Simone Martini: Annunciation", "Simone Martini", 1333, "Tempera and gold on panel", "Italian Gothic", ["gothic","gold","graceful","religious","elegant"], ["Angel Gabriel","Virgin Mary","lily","annunciation","golden"], ["gold","blue","red","white","lily"], "Uffizi Gallery, Florence", "The Angel Gabriel with polychrome wings announces to the Virgin, who recoils slightly, the entire composition edged with pointed Gothic arches.", "One of the supreme masterpieces of Italian Gothic painting. The elegant line, gold ground, and psychological tension between Gabriel and Mary are unmatched.", "male", "Italian"),
    ("Duccio: Maestà (front panel)", "Duccio di Buoninsegna", 1311, "Tempera and gold on panel", "Proto-Renaissance / Italian Gothic", ["gold","hieratic","religious","formal","devotional"], ["Virgin Mary","Christ child","saints","angels","golden throne"], ["gold","blue","red","cream"], "Museo dell'Opera del Duomo, Siena", "The Virgin enthroned in majesty with Christ child on her lap, surrounded by angels and saints in hierarchical gold-ground composition.", "The first great masterpiece of Sienese painting. Duccio's humanity softened Byzantine rigidity. Carried through Siena in procession on completion.", "male", "Italian"),
    ("Giotto: Lamentation of Christ (Scrovegni Chapel)", "Giotto di Bondone", 1305, "Fresco", "Proto-Renaissance / Italian", ["fresco","dramatic","emotional","revolutionary","spatial"], ["lamentation","Christ","Virgin Mary","grief","angels","sky"], ["blue sky","red","white","grey","earthy tones"], "Scrovegni Chapel, Padua", "The dead Christ is mourned by the Virgin and disciples. Grieving angels fill the sky above. The rocky hill creates a stage for human grief.", "A revolution in Western art. Giotto's spatial depth, psychological realism, and emotional intensity broke decisively with Byzantine conventions.", "male", "Italian"),
    ("Cimabue: Crucifix", "Cimabue", 1287, "Tempera on panel", "Proto-Renaissance / Italian", ["religious","monumental","gold","hieratic","transitional"], ["crucified Christ","cross","mourning figures","gold","Byzantine"], ["gold","blue","red","dark"], "Museo dell'Opera di Santa Croce, Florence", "Christ on the cross with mourning figures at each end, the body already slightly bent in a naturalistic arc away from pure Byzantine convention.", "The Cimabue Crucifix was severely damaged in the 1966 Florence flood. Giotto was supposedly Cimabue's student. A bridge between Byzantine and Renaissance.", "male", "Italian"),

    # ── EARLY NETHERLANDISH & NORTHERN EUROPEAN ───────────────────────────
    ("Ghent Altarpiece", "Hubert and Jan van Eyck", 1432, "Oil on oak panel (polyptych)", "Early Netherlandish / Northern Renaissance", ["polyptych","religious","monumental","detailed","luminous"], ["Adoration of the Lamb","God","Virgin","angels","pilgrims","paradise"], ["rich green","gold","blue","red","luminous"], "St Bavo's Cathedral, Ghent", "A multi-panel altarpiece showing the Adoration of the Mystic Lamb in paradise, with God enthroned flanked by Virgin and John the Baptist.", "Called the 'beginning of Flemish painting'. The earliest surviving major oil painting. Stolen and recovered repeatedly; subject of an entire WWII operation.", "male", "Flemish"),
    ("Rogier van der Weyden: Descent from the Cross", "Rogier van der Weyden", 1435, "Oil on panel", "Early Netherlandish", ["emotional","gold ground","sculptural","religious","intense"], ["Christ","Virgin","deposition","grief","apostles"], ["gold background","red","blue","white","flesh"], "Museo del Prado, Madrid", "Ten figures support the body of Christ in a shallow sculptural space against a flat gold ground, each expression of grief individualized.", "The most emotionally powerful Netherlandish altarpiece. The formal devices — symmetry of the swooning Virgin mirroring the dead Christ — are unforgettable.", "male", "Flemish"),
    ("Petrus Christus: Portrait of a Young Woman", "Petrus Christus", 1470, "Oil on panel", "Early Netherlandish", ["portrait","interior","luminous","detailed","symbolic"], ["young woman","headdress","white collar","interior","ledge"], ["dark background","cream","white","gold"], "Gemäldegalerie, Berlin", "A young woman in a white collar and black headdress in three-quarter view, the first Northern portrait set in a three-dimensional spatial box.", "Petrus Christus may have introduced the Northern portrait-in-interior format. Widely cited as the prototype for subsequent German and Flemish portraiture.", "male", "Flemish"),
    ("Hans Memling: Hans Memling Altarpiece (St John)", "Hans Memling", 1479, "Oil on panel (triptych)", "Early Netherlandish", ["religious","triptych","luminous","detailed","peaceful"], ["St John","baptism","Christ","saints","landscape"], ["green landscape","gold","blue","red","cream"], "St John's Hospital, Bruges", "A triptych showing the life and martyrdom of St John the Baptist and St John the Evangelist with luminous landscape backgrounds.", "Among the finest surviving Flemish altarpieces. Memling's serene figures and jewel-like color became the definitive image of Bruges piety.", "male", "German-Flemish"),
    ("Albrecht Dürer: Self-Portrait at 28", "Albrecht Dürer", 1500, "Oil on panel", "Northern Renaissance / German", ["self-portrait","frontal","detailed","symbolic","iconic"], ["self-portrait","fur coat","frontal gaze","Christ-like","hair"], ["dark background","brown fur","cream","flesh"], "Alte Pinakothek, Munich", "Dürer faces the viewer frontally in a pose borrowed from Christ Pantocrator, his right hand raised palm-forward, wearing a rich fur coat.", "The most unusual self-portrait of the Renaissance — Dürer placed himself in the divine frontal pose. A manifesto of the artist as equal to God.", "male", "German"),
    ("Albrecht Dürer: Four Horsemen of the Apocalypse", "Albrecht Dürer", 1498, "Woodblock print", "Northern Renaissance / German", ["woodblock","dramatic","apocalyptic","dynamic","powerful"], ["horsemen","apocalypse","biblical","death","war","famine","pestilence"], ["black","white","crosshatch"], "Various collections", "Four riders on horseback — War, Famine, Pestilence, and Death — trample the poor and the powerful alike.", "The most powerful image of Dürer's Apocalypse series. Transformed woodblock printing into a major artistic medium.", "male", "German"),
    ("Lucas Cranach the Elder: Venus", "Lucas Cranach the Elder", 1532, "Oil on panel", "Northern Renaissance / German", ["mannerist","elongated","nude","landscape","german"], ["Venus","nude","hat","necklace","landscape"], ["transparent veil","dark landscape","flesh","gold"], "Städel Museum, Frankfurt", "A pale, elongated Venus stands against a dark landscape wearing nothing but a wide-brimmed hat, necklace, and transparent veil.", "Cranach's Venus established a German Mannerist ideal of feminine beauty — elongated, pale, and ambiguously modest. A recurring image in his workshop.", "male", "German"),
    ("Matthias Grünewald: Isenheim Altarpiece", "Matthias Grünewald", 1516, "Oil on panel (polyptych)", "Northern Renaissance / German", ["expressionistic","gruesome","religious","dramatic","emotional"], ["crucifixion","Christ","wounds","plague","suffering"], ["dark","blood red","green","grey","golden light"], "Unterlinden Museum, Colmar", "The central panel shows Christ crucified with a twisted, tortured body covered in plague pustules. The wings open to reveal the Resurrection.", "Created for a hospital treating ergotism (St Anthony's Fire). Christ's diseased body was intended to comfort and identify with patients. Most expressive crucifixion ever.", "male", "German"),

    # ── ITALIAN RENAISSANCE CONTINUED ─────────────────────────────────────
    ("Botticelli: Primavera", "Sandro Botticelli", 1482, "Tempera on panel", "Early Renaissance / Florentine", ["mythological","decorative","linear","spring","allegorical"], ["Venus","Three Graces","Mercury","Zephyr","Spring flowers"], ["green forest","pink","orange","white","gold"], "Uffizi Gallery, Florence", "Nine mythological figures in an orange grove celebrate spring. Venus presides over the Three Graces dancing, Mercury, Zephyr, and the nymph Chloris.", "The most debated painting of the Renaissance for its iconography. A complex Neoplatonic allegory of love, beauty, and spring.", "male", "Italian"),
    ("Leonardo da Vinci: Virgin of the Rocks", "Leonardo da Vinci", 1483, "Oil on panel", "High Renaissance / Italian", ["sfumato","mysterious","religious","grotto","atmospheric"], ["Virgin Mary","infant Christ","infant John","angel","rocks"], ["dark grotto","blue","green","warm flesh"], "Louvre Museum, Paris", "The Virgin Mary shelters the infant Christ and infant John the Baptist in a rocky grotto, with an angel pointing to John.", "Demonstrates Leonardo's revolutionary sfumato and his scientific observation of geology. The London and Paris versions differ in key ways still debated.", "male", "Italian"),
    ("Raphael: Madonna of the Meadow", "Raphael", 1506, "Oil on panel", "High Renaissance / Florentine", ["classical","serene","balanced","religious","pyramidal"], ["Virgin Mary","Christ child","infant John","meadow","landscape"], ["blue","red","green","warm flesh","blue sky"], "Kunsthistorisches Museum, Vienna", "The Virgin forms a stable triangle with the two infant figures in a serene open meadow with a luminous blue landscape behind.", "The perfect expression of High Renaissance harmony and balance. Raphael synthesized Leonardo's pyramid composition with a new serene sweetness.", "male", "Italian"),
    ("Titian: Venus with a Mirror", "Titian", 1555, "Oil on canvas", "Renaissance / Venetian", ["sensuous","warm","reflective","female nude","venetian"], ["Venus","mirror","cupids","jewels","reflection"], ["warm flesh","red","dark velvet","gold"], "National Gallery of Art, Washington D.C.", "Venus holds up a mirror held by two Cupids while a second Cupid crowns her with a laurel wreath. She regards herself with composed pleasure.", "Titian's late Venus paintings established the model for Rubens, Velázquez, and later European nude painting. The warm Venetian palette is matchless.", "male", "Italian"),
    ("Parmigianino: Madonna with the Long Neck", "Parmigianino", 1540, "Oil on panel", "Mannerism / Italian", ["mannerist","elongated","elegant","strange","graceful"], ["Madonna","long neck","sleeping Christ child","angels","column"], ["pale flesh","red","cream","cold light"], "Uffizi Gallery, Florence", "The Virgin Mary's neck is elongated to impossible elegance. The sleeping Christ child lies across her lap like a dead adult. A column in the background leads nowhere.", "The paradigm of Italian Mannerism. The elegant distortions are entirely deliberate. Left unfinished at Parmigianino's death.", "male", "Italian"),
    ("Michelangelo: David", "Michelangelo", 1504, "Marble sculpture", "High Renaissance / Italian", ["monumental","classical","ideal","heroic","nude"], ["David","young hero","tension","ideal body","before battle"], ["white marble"], "Galleria dell'Accademia, Florence", "The biblical David stands in contrapposto, muscles tense, eyes fixed on Goliath. He holds his sling over his left shoulder.", "The supreme achievement of Renaissance sculpture. 5.17 meters of Carrara marble. David before the battle — a psychological as well as physical ideal.", "male", "Italian"),
    ("Michelangelo: Pietà", "Michelangelo", 1499, "Marble sculpture", "High Renaissance / Italian", ["religious","tender","detailed","monumental","classical"], ["Virgin Mary","Christ","lamentation","death","marble"], ["white marble"], "St Peter's Basilica, Vatican", "The Virgin Mary holds the body of the dead Christ across her lap with serene maternal composure.", "The only work Michelangelo ever signed — his name across Mary's sash. Carved when he was 24. The technical virtuosity and emotional restraint are unique.", "male", "Italian"),
    ("Caravaggio: Supper at Emmaus", "Caravaggio", 1601, "Oil on canvas", "Baroque / Italian", ["chiaroscuro","dramatic","realistic","biblical","tenebrism"], ["Christ","disciples","revelation","supper","inn"], ["dark background","dramatic light","warm flesh","food"], "National Gallery, London", "The risen Christ blesses bread at an inn. Two disciples recognize him and throw out their arms in astonishment.", "A masterwork of Caravaggio's tenebrism. The disciples' gestures burst beyond the picture frame. Christ is beardless — still a young man.", "male", "Italian"),
    ("Caravaggio: The Calling of Saint Matthew", "Caravaggio", 1600, "Oil on canvas", "Baroque / Italian", ["chiaroscuro","dramatic","biblical","light beam","realistic"], ["Matthew","Christ","tax collector","divine light","pointing"], ["dark interior","shaft of light","brown clothes"], "San Luigi dei Francesi, Rome", "A beam of light cuts through a dark room where Matthew and his companions count money. Christ's pointing hand summons Matthew.", "One of Caravaggio's greatest works. The beam of divine light, realized as the natural sunlight of the composition, was unprecedented.", "male", "Italian"),
    ("Annibale Carracci: Loves of the Gods (Farnese Gallery ceiling)", "Annibale Carracci", 1601, "Fresco", "Baroque / Italian", ["baroque","ceiling fresco","mythological","classical","illusionistic"], ["Venus","Bacchus","Mercury","gods","loves","ceiling"], ["warm flesh","blue sky","gold","architectural frame"], "Palazzo Farnese, Rome", "A vast ceiling fresco showing the loves of the ancient gods framed in simulated architectural cartouches and herms.", "The first major Baroque ceiling fresco. Carracci's illusionistic architectural frames inspired a century of European ceiling painting.", "male", "Italian"),
    ("Giovanni Battista Tiepolo: Banquet of Cleopatra", "Giovanni Battista Tiepolo", 1743, "Oil on canvas", "Venetian Baroque / Rococo", ["rococo","theatrical","colorful","luminous","historical"], ["Cleopatra","banquet","Anthony","pearl","luxury"], ["warm yellow","blue","marble","silk","theatrical light"], "National Gallery of Victoria, Melbourne", "Cleopatra drops a pearl into a cup of vinegar to dissolve it, winning a bet with Marc Anthony about who can host the most expensive banquet.", "Tiepolo's luminous palette and theatrical composition are at their most glorious. One of three versions; the Melbourne canvas is the largest.", "male", "Italian"),
    ("Canaletto: The Grand Canal with Santa Maria della Salute", "Canaletto", 1744, "Oil on canvas", "Venetian / Vedute", ["veduta","urban","luminous","architectural","precise"], ["Venice","Grand Canal","church","gondolas","water","blue sky"], ["blue","white","warm stone","turquoise water"], "Woburn Abbey, England", "The Grand Canal opens toward the dome of Santa Maria della Salute, gondolas and traghetti crossing the sunlit water.", "Canaletto's vedute defined Venice for the world. Painted for the Grand Tour market. His precision and luminosity are unique in cityscape painting.", "male", "Italian"),
    ("Francesco Guardi: Piazza San Marco", "Francesco Guardi", 1760, "Oil on canvas", "Venetian / Vedute", ["veduta","atmospheric","looser","romantic","city scene"], ["Venice","Piazza San Marco","crowds","architecture","atmosphere"], ["grey blue","warm stone","crowd colors"], "Uffizi Gallery, Florence", "The vast Piazza San Marco with the Basilica and Campanile, crowds of tiny figures moving through the sunlit square.", "Guardi's looser, more atmospheric style contrasts with Canaletto's precision. His flickering light anticipates Impressionism.", "male", "Italian"),

    # ── SPANISH & LATIN AMERICAN ───────────────────────────────────────────
    ("Velázquez: The Rokeby Venus", "Diego Velázquez", 1651, "Oil on canvas", "Baroque / Spanish", ["nude","reflective","sensual","back view","subtle"], ["Venus","mirror","cupid","reclining nude","reflection"], ["warm flesh","grey-blue","red silk","dark"], "National Gallery, London", "Venus reclines with her back to the viewer, looking at herself in a mirror held by Cupid. Her reflection is deliberately blurred.", "The only surviving female nude by Velázquez. Slashed by suffragette Mary Richardson in 1914. The blurred reflection denies us Venus's face.", "male", "Spanish"),
    ("Goya: The Sleep of Reason Produces Monsters", "Francisco Goya", 1799, "Aquatint and etching", "Romanticism / Spanish", ["dark","satirical","etching","nightmarish","symbolic"], ["sleeping man","owls","bats","darkness","reason"], ["dark black","white","grey"], "Museo del Prado, Madrid", "A man slumps asleep at his desk while owls and bats swarm behind him. The caption reads: 'The sleep of reason produces monsters.'", "From the Caprichos series — Goya's satirical attack on superstition and irrationality. One of the most quoted images in Western art.", "male", "Spanish"),
    ("Goya: Witches' Sabbath (Black Paintings)", "Francisco Goya", 1823, "Oil mural on plaster", "Romanticism / Spanish", ["dark","occult","nightmarish","expressionistic","psychological"], ["witches","devil goat","gathering","night","horror"], ["dark","brown","black","pale faces"], "Museo del Prado, Madrid", "A horned goat presides over a gathering of witches and hags in a moonlit night scene of disturbing intensity.", "One of the 'Black Paintings' Goya painted directly on the walls of his house at Quinta del Sordo. The most disturbing image from the series.", "male", "Spanish"),
    ("Rivera: Dream of a Sunday Afternoon in Alameda Park", "Diego Rivera", 1947, "Fresco", "Mexican Muralism", ["mural","historical","colorful","panoramic","social"], ["figures","history","park","Sunday","crowd"], ["green","brown","colorful clothes","sky"], "Museo Mural Diego Rivera, Mexico City", "A 15-meter panoramic fresco shows 400 years of Mexican history with historical figures strolling in Alameda Park.", "Rivera's greatest fresco and most autobiographical work. He appears as a child; Kahlo stands behind him. Damaged in the 1985 earthquake.", "male", "Mexican"),
    ("José Clemente Orozco: The Epic of American Civilization (detail: Quetzalcoatl)", "José Clemente Orozco", 1934, "Fresco", "Mexican Muralism", ["mural","monumental","social realist","dark","powerful"], ["Quetzalcoatl","civilization","indigenous","serpent god","departure"], ["earthy red","dark","golden light","geometric"], "Baker Library, Dartmouth College", "The feathered serpent Quetzalcoatl departs from the people of Mesoamerica in a panel from Orozco's 24-panel Dartmouth fresco cycle.", "Orozco's Dartmouth cycle is the most powerful anti-imperialist mural in North America. His dark expressionism contrasts sharply with Rivera's optimism.", "male", "Mexican"),
    ("Remedios Varo: Still Life by Moonlight", "Remedios Varo", 1956, "Oil on hardboard", "Surrealism / Mexican", ["surrealist","dreamlike","intricate","mysterious","metaphysical"], ["moonlight","fruit","table","glass","mysterious glow"], ["blue moonlight","green","cream","dark"], "Private collection", "A table set with food and glass in moonlight; the items begin to levitate and transform in a quiet nocturnal surrealism.", "Varo's unique surrealism combined meticulous craft with a feminine, alchemical imagination. Her work is celebrated in Mexico as a national treasure.", "female", "Spanish-Mexican"),
    ("Leonora Carrington: The Pomps of the Subsoil", "Leonora Carrington", 1947, "Oil on canvas", "Surrealism / Mexican", ["surrealist","symbolic","fantastical","ritual","personal"], ["hybrid creatures","underground","procession","alchemy","mythology"], ["dark","cream","brown","mystical light"], "National Museum of Art, Mexico City", "Strange hybrid creatures process through an underground realm in a ritual that mixes Celtic myth, alchemy, and surrealist transformation.", "Carrington's most ambitious early canvas. Her visual world — part medieval bestiary, part personal mythology — is entirely her own.", "female", "British-Mexican"),

    # ── FRENCH 17TH–18TH CENTURIES ────────────────────────────────────────
    ("Nicolas Poussin: Et in Arcadia Ego", "Nicolas Poussin", 1637, "Oil on canvas", "French Classicism", ["classical","meditative","allegorical","landscape","stoic"], ["shepherds","tomb","Latin inscription","Arcadia","death"], ["golden light","green","blue","warm brown"], "Louvre Museum, Paris", "Three shepherds and a woman contemplate a tomb bearing the Latin inscription 'Et in Arcadia Ego' — even in Arcadia, I (Death) am present.", "The paradigmatic image of memento mori in a classical landscape. The phrase 'Et in Arcadia Ego' became a touchstone of European culture.", "male", "French"),
    ("Claude Lorrain: Landscape with the Marriage of Isaac and Rebekah", "Claude Lorrain", 1648, "Oil on canvas", "French Classicism / Landscape", ["classical landscape","golden light","pastoral","atmospheric","idyllic"], ["biblical","river","dancing figures","trees","golden horizon"], ["golden light","blue sky","green trees","warm tones"], "National Gallery, London", "A wedding celebration in a pastoral landscape glowing with the warm light of late afternoon. Trees frame the vast sky.", "Claude's greatest landscape. Turner specifically requested to be buried next to it. Defined the 'Claudian' ideal of classical landscape.", "male", "French"),
    ("Jean-Siméon Chardin: The Ray (La Raie)", "Jean-Siméon Chardin", 1728, "Oil on canvas", "French Realism / Still Life", ["still life","realistic","humble","quiet","textured"], ["ray fish","cat","oysters","kitchen","table"], ["silver","red entrails","grey","warm light"], "Louvre Museum, Paris", "A gutted ray hangs on a kitchen wall, its viscera exposed in grotesque naturalism, while a cat crouches below.", "Chardin's debut masterpiece. Diderot wrote that it made him 'uneasy before Nature herself'. The ray's entrails suggest a monstrous face.", "male", "French"),
    ("Jean-Honoré Fragonard: The Progress of Love (The Meeting)", "Jean-Honoré Fragonard", 1771, "Oil on canvas", "Rococo / French", ["rococo","romantic","garden","luminous","pastel"], ["lovers","garden wall","roses","secret meeting","youth"], ["green","white","pink","soft gold"], "Frick Collection, New York", "A young man vaults over a garden wall to meet his beloved who waits with roses and a look of surprise and delight.", "Part of a series commissioned by Madame du Barry and refused by her. The most virtuoso examples of Rococo garden romance.", "male", "French"),
    ("Édouard Vuillard: Mother and Sister of the Artist", "Édouard Vuillard", 1893, "Oil on canvas", "Post-Impressionism / Intimisme", ["intimate","patterned","decorative","domestic","quiet"], ["mother","sister","interior","wallpaper","domestic"], ["red","green","pattern","muted tones"], "Museum of Modern Art, MoMA", "Two women in a domestic interior merge with the patterned wallpaper and fabric behind them in a flat, intimate composition.", "Vuillard's 'intimisme' reduced interior painting to pattern and atmosphere. His domestic scenes are among the most quietly radical works of the 1890s.", "male", "French"),
    ("Pierre Bonnard: The Breakfast Room", "Pierre Bonnard", 1930, "Oil on canvas", "Post-Impressionism / French", ["colorful","domestic","luminous","patterned","intimate"], ["breakfast","interior","table","window","light"], ["warm yellow","cream","blue","patterned cloth"], "Museum of Modern Art, MoMA", "A sun-flooded breakfast room with a set table and an open window overlooking a garden, drenched in Bonnard's characteristic warm color.", "Bonnard remained deeply personal and chromatic when his contemporaries went abstract. Matisse called him 'the most painterly of painters'.", "male", "French"),

    # ── GERMAN & AUSTRIAN EXPRESSIONISM ───────────────────────────────────
    ("Ernst Ludwig Kirchner: Street, Berlin", "Ernst Ludwig Kirchner", 1913, "Oil on canvas", "Expressionism / Die Brücke", ["expressionist","urban","angular","alienated","harsh color"], ["Berlin street","women","crowded","urban anxiety","movement"], ["pink","black","dark green","harsh light"], "Museum of Modern Art, MoMA", "Two women walk along a Berlin street, their elongated angular forms pressing through a crowd. The harsh colors create urban unease.", "One of Kirchner's Berlin street scenes — a pivotal series capturing the anxiety of modernity. His later expressionism darkened after WWI shell shock.", "male", "German"),
    ("Egon Schiele: The Embrace (Lovers II)", "Egon Schiele", 1917, "Oil on canvas", "Expressionism / Austrian", ["expressionist","raw","intimate","angular","psychological"], ["couple","embrace","nude","floor","intimate"], ["orange","cream","flesh","earthy"], "Österreichische Galerie Belvedere, Vienna", "Two figures cling together on a white sheet, their angular bodies creating an intense, raw image of physical and emotional union.", "One of Schiele's most tender large paintings. He died at 28 in the 1918 flu pandemic, three days after his pregnant wife.", "male", "Austrian"),
    ("Oskar Kokoschka: The Bride of the Wind", "Oskar Kokoschka", 1914, "Oil on canvas", "Expressionism / Austrian", ["expressionist","turbulent","romantic","stormy","psychological"], ["couple","storm","swirling","love","conflict"], ["blue","grey","white","dark swirling"], "Kunstmuseum Basel", "Kokoschka and his lover Alma Mahler lie in a boat tossed on a stormy sea, he awake and anguished, she asleep and calm.", "A monument of Expressionist painting and personal mythology. After Alma Mahler ended the relationship, Kokoschka had a life-size doll made of her.", "male", "Austrian"),
    ("Max Beckmann: Departure (Triptych)", "Max Beckmann", 1935, "Oil on canvas (triptych)", "Expressionism / German", ["expressionist","dark","allegorical","triptych","powerful"], ["torture","war","departure","sea","freedom","myth"], ["dark","red","blue sea","gold","symbolic"], "Museum of Modern Art, MoMA", "The two wing panels show scenes of torture and bondage; the central panel shows a royal departure by sea in bright blue light.", "Beckmann's coded critique of Nazism. He fled Germany the day after Hitler's 1937 speech denouncing degenerate art. A masterpiece of political allegory.", "male", "German"),
    ("Paul Klee: Twittering Machine", "Paul Klee", 1922, "Watercolor and pen on oil transfer drawing", "Expressionism / Bauhaus", ["abstract","whimsical","mechanical","line","humor"], ["birds","machine","crank","abstract","satire"], ["pale blue","line drawing","watercolor washes"], "Museum of Modern Art, MoMA", "Four bird-like figures perched on a wire connected to a hand crank — a satirical mechanical contraption of song.", "Klee's playful irony about the mechanization of nature. The title and image together satirize industrial modernity and the reduction of beauty to mechanism.", "male", "German-Swiss"),
    ("Wassily Kandinsky: Composition VIII", "Wassily Kandinsky", 1923, "Oil on canvas", "Abstract / Bauhaus", ["abstract","geometric","colorful","musical","spiritual"], ["circles","triangles","lines","color","pure abstraction"], ["red","blue","yellow","black","white"], "Solomon R. Guggenheim Museum, New York", "An orchestration of geometric shapes — circles, arcs, grid lines — in vivid primary colors across a light ground.", "The first fully abstract paintings in Western art were Kandinsky's. Composition VIII shows his Bauhaus turn from organic to geometric abstraction.", "male", "Russian"),
    ("Lyonel Feininger: The Cathedral (Bauhaus Manifesto woodcut)", "Lyonel Feininger", 1919, "Woodblock print", "Expressionism / Bauhaus", ["expressionist","architectural","angular","woodblock","symbolic"], ["cathedral","rays of light","crystalline","geometric","Gothic"], ["black","white","crosshatch"], "Various collections", "A crystalline Gothic cathedral radiates beams of light in a dynamic Expressionist woodblock print.", "Created as the frontispiece for the founding Bauhaus manifesto in 1919. The crystalline cathedral became the symbol of the Bauhaus ideal.", "male", "German-American"),

    # ── 20TH CENTURY AMERICAN ─────────────────────────────────────────────
    ("Georgia O'Keeffe: Black Iris", "Georgia O'Keeffe", 1926, "Oil on canvas", "American Modernism", ["sensuous","close-up","abstract","floral","intimate"], ["iris","dark petals","abstract form","close-up","female"], ["black","purple","cream","dark violet"], "Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York", "An extreme close-up of a dark iris magnified to fill the entire canvas, its petals unfolding in a dark, sensuous abstraction.", "O'Keeffe's flower paintings operate between the intimate and the abstract. Critics saw sexual symbolism she denied. The scale transforms botanics into landscape.", "female", "American"),
    ("Georgia O'Keeffe: Ram's Head White Hollyhock and Little Hills", "Georgia O'Keeffe", 1935, "Oil on canvas", "American Modernism", ["desert","surreal","bones","flowers","southwest"], ["ram skull","flower","hills","New Mexico","bones"], ["cream","pink","blue","white","desert"], "Brooklyn Museum", "A ram's skull floats against the pink and blue hills of New Mexico with a white hollyhock blossom beside it.", "O'Keeffe's New Mexico bones series transformed desert death into serene beauty. Her desert subjects defined the American Southwest landscape.", "female", "American"),
    ("Stuart Davis: Owh! In San Paõ", "Stuart Davis", 1951, "Oil on canvas", "American Modernism / Abstract", ["jazz","abstract","colorful","flat","modern"], ["jazz","abstract shapes","text","color","rhythm"], ["red","blue","yellow","black","white"], "Whitney Museum, New York", "Bold patches of color and letter fragments create a visual jazz riff on an urban environment.", "Davis translated jazz music into visual equivalents. His work bridged Cubism and American Pop Art, influencing a generation of younger American painters.", "male", "American"),
    ("Horace Pippin: John Brown Going to His Hanging", "Horace Pippin", 1942, "Oil on panel", "African American / Self-taught", ["self-taught","historical","powerful","stark","narrative"], ["John Brown","hanging","crowd","winter","dignity"], ["dark tree","snow","crowd","wagon"], "Pennsylvania Academy of Fine Arts", "John Brown rides to his hanging in a wagon through a winter landscape. His expression is serene; the watching crowd is hushed.", "Pippin was a self-taught African American artist and WWI veteran. His Civil War and historical paintings are visionary moral documents.", "male", "American"),
    ("Jacob Lawrence: Migration Series #1", "Jacob Lawrence", 1940, "Casein tempera on hardboard", "African American / Social Realism", ["flat","graphic","geometric","social","narrative"], ["migration","workers","crowd","train station","movement"], ["grey","brown","red","black","flat pattern"], "Museum of Modern Art, MoMA", "Masses of figures crowd around train and bus departure boards in a flat, powerful graphic statement of the Great Migration.", "Lawrence's 60-panel series documents the migration of African Americans from the rural South to the urban North. A landmark of American social art.", "male", "American"),
    ("Lee Krasner: Noon", "Lee Krasner", 1947, "Oil on canvas", "Abstract Expressionism / American", ["abstract","gestural","dense","fragmented","powerful"], ["broken images","dense marks","collage","cut paper"], ["earth brown","cream","dark","ochre"], "Private collection", "A dense composition of Krasner's own destroyed earlier drawings cut and reorganized into a new painterly whole.", "Krasner destroyed and reinvented herself repeatedly. This 'Little Image' series predates Pollock's drip work and shows her independent formal invention.", "female", "American"),
    ("Helen Frankenthaler: Mountains and Sea", "Helen Frankenthaler", 1952, "Oil and charcoal on canvas", "Abstract Expressionism / Color Field", ["color field","stained","luminous","lyrical","large scale"], ["landscape","color wash","poured paint","sea","mountains"], ["pale pink","blue","green","lavender","transparent wash"], "National Gallery of Art, Washington D.C.", "Washes of thinned paint stained directly into unprimed canvas create luminous, translucent landscape color fields.", "Frankenthaler's soak-stain technique directly inspired Morris Louis and Kenneth Noland. The work bridges Abstract Expressionism and Color Field.", "female", "American"),
    ("Cy Twombly: Leda and the Swan", "Cy Twombly", 1962, "Oil, pencil, crayon on canvas", "Abstract Expressionism / American", ["gestural","mythological","scrawl","sensuous","raw"], ["scrawl","mythological","pencil marks","raw paint","eros"], ["grey","cream","pencil grey","red scrawl"], "Museum of Modern Art, MoMA", "Looping pencil marks and smears of white paint evoke the mythological union of Zeus-as-swan and Leda through pure gestural suggestion.", "Twombly's mythological paintings collapse classical narrative into scrawl and gesture. He was alternately reviled and worshipped for their deliberate rawness.", "male", "American"),
    ("Robert Rauschenberg: Bed", "Robert Rauschenberg", 1955, "Oil and pencil on pillow, quilt, and sheet", "Neo-Dada / American", ["neo-dada","combine painting","domestic object","paint","radical"], ["bed","quilt","pillow","paint drips","found object"], ["red","cream","white","paint drips"], "Museum of Modern Art, MoMA", "A real pillow and bed quilt mounted upright like a canvas, splattered with expressionistic paint.", "When Rauschenberg could not afford canvas, he painted on his own bedding. Launched the 'Combine painting' — a radical fusion of painting and sculpture.", "male", "American"),
    ("Jasper Johns: Flag", "Jasper Johns", 1955, "Encaustic and collage on canvas", "Neo-Dada / Pop Art", ["neo-dada","flat","iconic","encaustic","ambiguous"], ["American flag","stars","stripes","image as object"], ["red","white","blue","newsprint texture"], "Museum of Modern Art, MoMA", "The American flag rendered in encaustic wax, exactly the size of the canvas, so the flag becomes neither representation nor object but both simultaneously.", "Johns asked: what is a painting if the subject and the support are the same? One of the most conceptually loaded images in American art.", "male", "American"),
    ("Barnett Newman: Vir Heroicus Sublimis", "Barnett Newman", 1951, "Oil on canvas", "Abstract Expressionism / Color Field", ["color field","monumental","minimal","sublime","large scale"], ["vast red","zip","color","sublime","confrontation"], ["cadmium red","thin white zips","vast"], "Museum of Modern Art, MoMA", "A vast, almost 6-meter field of cadmium red interrupted by five thin vertical 'zips' in varied colors.", "Newman's 'zips' were his signature device — the sublime created through scale and pure color. Intended to be experienced from 18 inches away.", "male", "American"),
    ("Franz Kline: Painting Number 2", "Franz Kline", 1954, "Oil on canvas", "Abstract Expressionism / American", ["gestural","black and white","bold","abstract","urban"], ["black brushstrokes","white ground","structural","steel"], ["black","white"], "Museum of Modern Art, MoMA", "Massive black brushstrokes cross the canvas like steel girders. The white ground is as active as the black marks.", "Kline's large black-and-white abstractions evoke the industrial structure of American cities. Their power is entirely in the balance of mark and space.", "male", "American"),
    ("Philip Guston: The Studio", "Philip Guston", 1969, "Oil on canvas", "Neo-Expressionism / American", ["expressionist","figurative","cartoon-like","autobiographical","dark humor"], ["hooded figure","painter","studio","cigarette","shoes","bulbous"], ["pink","flesh","dark","red","black"], "Museum of Modern Art, MoMA", "A hooded Klan figure (self-portrait of the artist) sits in a studio painting small hooded heads on a canvas.", "When Guston returned to figuration in 1969, the art world was scandalized. His 'Late Work' is now recognized as among the bravest in American art.", "male", "American"),
    ("Jean-Michel Basquiat: Untitled (Skull)", "Jean-Michel Basquiat", 1981, "Acrylic and oil stick on canvas", "Neo-Expressionism / American", ["neo-expressionist","raw","graffiti","text","urban"], ["skull","crown","text","graffiti","urban","race"], ["black","cream","gold crown","red text"], "Various private collections", "A fragmented skull with a three-pointed crown above, surrounded by cryptic text and paint marks.", "Basquiat's skull series confronted race, death, and identity in the art world. The three-pointed crown became his trademark symbol.", "male", "American"),
    ("Keith Haring: Untitled (Three Dancing Figures)", "Keith Haring", 1983, "Vinyl paint on vinyl tarpaulin", "Pop Art / Street Art", ["pop","urban","dynamic","line","public art"], ["dancing figures","bold outlines","movement","joy","public space"], ["red","black outlines","white ground"], "Various collections", "Three bold cartoon-like figures dance in a continuous line with radiating marks of energy from their joints.", "Haring began drawing in the New York subway on blank advertising panels. His bold, joyful figures became global symbols of public art and AIDS activism.", "male", "American"),

    # ── BRITISH ART ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    ("William Blake: The Ancient of Days", "William Blake", 1794, "Relief etching with watercolor", "Romanticism / British", ["romantic","visionary","symbolic","mystical","human figure"], ["God","compass","energy","divine geometer","cosmos"], ["gold","blue","white","dramatic"], "British Museum, London", "A white-haired figure leans from a circle of light to measure the cosmos with golden compasses.", "Blake's most recognized image. He printed and painted it repeatedly throughout his life. Represents the false god of rational measurement versus spiritual imagination.", "male", "British"),
    ("Pre-Raphaelite: Ophelia", "John Everett Millais", 1852, "Oil on canvas", "Pre-Raphaelitism / British", ["pre-raphaelite","detailed","romantic","tragic","naturalistic"], ["Ophelia","floating","flowers","water","Shakespeare"], ["green","cream","brown","floral","water"], "Tate Britain, London", "Ophelia sings as she drowns, floating in a stream surrounded by flowers, each painted with botanical precision.", "The model Elizabeth Siddal lay in a cold bath for months to pose. Millais painted the stream's vegetation in microscopic detail. A Pre-Raphaelite touchstone.", "male", "British"),
    ("John Singer Sargent: Carnation Lily Lily Rose", "John Singer Sargent", 1886, "Oil on canvas", "Impressionism / British", ["impressionistic","luminous","atmospheric","children","garden"], ["children","lanterns","garden","evening light","lilies"], ["warm orange","white","green","twilight"], "Tate Britain, London", "Two girls in white dresses light paper lanterns in a garden at twilight, surrounded by lilies and roses.", "Sargent painted it outdoors during a narrow window of twilight light each day over two years. The most celebrated painting in Victorian Britain.", "male", "American"),
    ("L.S. Lowry: Coming from the Mill", "L.S. Lowry", 1930, "Oil on canvas", "British Modernism", ["industrial","social","urban","flat","northern"], ["mill workers","matchstick figures","smoke","industrial town","crowds"], ["grey","white","black smoke","muted"], "The Lowry, Salford", "Crowds of matchstick figures stream from mill gates against a smoky grey sky filled with factory chimneys.", "Lowry's industrial Lancashire scenes were initially dismissed. Now recognized as unique social documents of British working-class life.", "male", "British"),
    ("Francis Bacon: Study after Velázquez's Portrait of Pope Innocent X", "Francis Bacon", 1953, "Oil on canvas", "Expressionism / British", ["expressionist","psychological","distorted","screaming","confined"], ["screaming pope","blurred","chair","curtain","velazquez"], ["purple","cream","dark background","flesh"], "Des Moines Art Center", "A Pope figure, derived from Velázquez's portrait, opens his mouth in a silent scream, his image smeared and distorted by paint.", "Bacon's 'Screaming Popes' are among the most psychologically violent images in 20th-century art. He refused to explain them.", "male", "Irish-British"),
    ("Lucian Freud: Benefits Supervisor Sleeping", "Lucian Freud", 1995, "Oil on canvas", "Figurative / British", ["figurative","unflinching","realistic","flesh","psychological"], ["sleeping woman","large figure","sofa","nude","raw"], ["flesh","cream sofa","warm","unflinching realism"], "Private collection", "A large woman sleeps nude on a low sofa. Freud renders every fold of skin and imperfection with total, unsentimental attention.", "Sold for $33.6 million in 2008 — a record at the time for a living artist. Freud's total refusal of idealization was both offensive and awe-inspiring.", "male", "German-British"),
    ("Peter Doig: Blotter", "Peter Doig", 1993, "Oil on canvas", "Contemporary Figurative / British", ["figurative","dreamlike","landscape","reflective","atmospheric"], ["figure","ice","snow","reflection","isolation"], ["white","grey","blue","reflective surface","winter"], "Walker Art Gallery, Liverpool", "A solitary figure stands on a frozen lake whose icy surface reflects trees and grey sky with unsettling clarity.", "Doig's hypnagogic landscapes hover between dream and memory. This work helped launch his career and redefined late-20th-century figurative painting.", "male", "British"),

    # ── SCANDINAVIAN ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    ("Vilhelm Hammershøi: Interior with a Woman Standing", "Vilhelm Hammershøi", 1908, "Oil on canvas", "Symbolism / Danish", ["quiet","interior","grey","solitary","atmospheric"], ["woman","interior","back turned","door","light"], ["grey","cream","white","pale light"], "Various collections", "A woman stands with her back to the viewer in a spare grey interior, a door partially open to the next room.", "Hammershøi's grey interiors are meditation chambers. His recurring back-turned woman is never explained — she simply is. Influenced by Vermeer.", "male", "Danish"),
    ("Carl Larsson: The Garden Room", "Carl Larsson", 1894, "Watercolor", "Decorative / Swedish", ["domestic","colorful","idyllic","interior","warm"], ["family","garden room","light","furniture","Swedish house"], ["red","green","yellow","white","blue"], "National Museum of Sweden, Stockholm", "A sun-filled garden room in Larsson's home at Sundborn with his family at ease in cheerful, folk-art-inflected decoration.", "Larsson's home illustrations shaped the modern idea of the Swedish design aesthetic. His watercolors are among the most beloved in Scandinavian art.", "male", "Swedish"),
    ("Akseli Gallen-Kallela: The Defense of the Sampo", "Akseli Gallen-Kallela", 1896, "Tempera on canvas", "Symbolism / Finnish", ["symbolist","narrative","mythological","dramatic","Finnish"], ["Kalevala","hero","battle","eagle","sea"], ["dark","gold","blue sea","storm"], "Ateneum Art Museum, Helsinki", "The hero Väinämöinen and his companions battle the witch Louhi (transformed into an eagle) over the Sampo on a stormy sea.", "From the Finnish national epic Kalevala. Gallen-Kallela's Kalevala paintings are the visual foundation of Finnish national identity.", "male", "Finnish"),

    # ── RUSSIAN ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    ("Ilya Repin: Barge Haulers on the Volga", "Ilya Repin", 1873, "Oil on canvas", "Russian Realism", ["realist","social","powerful","panoramic","labor"], ["haulers","Volga","river","workers","harness"], ["golden Volga","dusty earth","sky","blue","brown"], "Russian Museum, St Petersburg", "Eleven men strain against their harnesses pulling a barge up the Volga in summer heat. Their faces are individualized portraits.", "The painting that established Russian Realism. A searing indictment of serfdom and labor. The men are known — Repin spent a summer with them.", "male", "Russian"),
    ("Kazimir Malevich: Black Square", "Kazimir Malevich", 1915, "Oil on canvas", "Suprematism / Russian", ["suprematist","minimal","radical","geometric","black"], ["black square","white ground","pure abstraction","zero","silence"], ["black","white"], "Tretyakov Gallery, Moscow", "A single black square on a white ground. Nothing more.", "Malevich called it 'the zero of form' — painting freed from any reference to the world. Shown at the 1915 Last Futurist Exhibition, hanging in the icon corner.", "male", "Russian"),
    ("Kazimir Malevich: Suprematist Composition (Red on Black)", "Kazimir Malevich", 1916, "Oil on canvas", "Suprematism / Russian", ["suprematist","geometric","dynamic","minimal","bold"], ["red rectangle","black","white ground","pure form"], ["red","black","white"], "Stedelijk Museum, Amsterdam", "A red rectangle tilts diagonally above a black rectangle on a white ground. Pure geometric force.", "One of the key works of Suprematism. The tilted rectangle creates dynamic tension out of pure geometric simplicity.", "male", "Russian"),
    ("El Lissitzky: Beat the Whites with the Red Wedge", "El Lissitzky", 1919, "Lithograph", "Constructivism / Russian", ["constructivist","propaganda","geometric","political","bold"], ["red triangle","white circle","propaganda","revolution","geometric"], ["red","white","black"], "Various collections", "A sharp red triangle (the Bolsheviks) pierces a white circle (the White Army) in this stark political poster.", "The most celebrated Constructivist poster. Lissitzky distilled political conflict into pure geometric form, making propaganda into art.", "male", "Russian"),
    ("Natalia Goncharova: Cats (Rayonist)", "Natalia Goncharova", 1913, "Oil on canvas", "Rayonism / Russian", ["rayonist","fragmented","dynamic","avant-garde","animal"], ["cats","rays of light","fragmented form","movement"], ["brown","cream","dark","radiating lines"], "Solomon R. Guggenheim Museum, New York", "Cats rendered in intersecting rays of light, their forms fragmented into glowing radiating lines.", "Goncharova's Rayonism depicted how objects project rays of reflected light. She was among the most radical artists in the Russian avant-garde.", "female", "Russian"),
    ("Alexander Rodchenko: Books (Please!) poster", "Alexander Rodchenko", 1925, "Lithograph", "Constructivism / Russian", ["constructivist","graphic design","bold","type","propaganda"], ["woman shouting","books","typography","red","dynamic"], ["red","black","white"], "Various collections", "A woman in profile shouts through cupped hands; the typography 'BOOKS (Please!) in all branches of knowledge' fills the design.", "Rodchenko's most famous poster, photographed with Lilya Brik (Mayakovsky's partner). The cropped photomontage aesthetic defined Soviet graphic design.", "male", "Russian"),

    # ── DUTCH 17TH CENTURY EXPANDED ───────────────────────────────────────
    ("Jan Steen: The Merry Family", "Jan Steen", 1668, "Oil on canvas", "Dutch Golden Age", ["genre","humorous","moralizing","domestic","lively"], ["family","singing","drinking","rowdy","domestic"], ["warm","red","brown","golden light","cluttered"], "Rijksmuseum, Amsterdam", "A boisterous family sings and drinks together. Children copy adult vices; the motto 'As the old sing, so the young twitter' is included.", "Steen's moralistic domestic comedies gave rise to the Dutch phrase 'Jan Steen household' meaning cheerful chaos. His humanism is unique in Dutch art.", "male", "Dutch"),
    ("Pieter de Hooch: The Courtyard of a House in Delft", "Pieter de Hooch", 1658, "Oil on canvas", "Dutch Golden Age", ["luminous","architectural","domestic","quiet","perspective"], ["courtyard","woman","child","brick","sunlight","doorway"], ["warm brick red","blue sky","white cloth","sunlight"], "National Gallery, London", "A woman and child stand at a doorway in a sunlit brick courtyard. Through the opening a further street scene is visible.", "De Hooch's layered spatial vistas and warm sunlight define the Delft domestic interior tradition alongside Vermeer. His courtyard scenes are serene masterworks.", "male", "Dutch"),
    ("Frans Hals: The Laughing Cavalier", "Frans Hals", 1624, "Oil on canvas", "Dutch Golden Age", ["portrait","lively","confident","embroidered","direct gaze"], ["cavalier","man","embroidered jacket","smiling","direct"], ["black","cream","gold embroidery","red"], "The Wallace Collection, London", "A young man in an elaborately embroidered black doublet looks at the viewer with a half-smile of supreme self-confidence.", "The most celebrated Dutch portrait after Rembrandt. Hals's liquid brushwork in the embroidered sleeve is technically without peer.", "male", "Dutch"),
    ("Jacob van Ruisdael: Jewish Cemetery", "Jacob van Ruisdael", 1654, "Oil on canvas", "Dutch Golden Age / Landscape", ["landscape","melancholic","atmospheric","symbolic","romantic"], ["cemetery","ruins","stormy sky","trees","graves"], ["grey","white","dark green","light breaking through"], "Gemäldegalerie, Dresden", "A Jewish cemetery with ruined tombs and dead trees beneath a stormy sky through which light breaks dramatically.", "The most emotionally powerful Dutch landscape. Goethe wrote about it at length. Transcends pure landscape painting into meditation on mortality.", "male", "Dutch"),

    # ── FRENCH REALISM & BARBIZON ─────────────────────────────────────────
    ("Gustave Courbet: The Stone Breakers", "Gustave Courbet", 1849, "Oil on canvas (destroyed in WWII)", "Realism / French", ["realist","social","monumental","labor","political"], ["workers","stone breaking","labor","poverty","rural"], ["brown","earth","golden light","grey"], "Destroyed (formerly Gemäldegalerie, Dresden)", "Two men break stones by the roadside — one old, one young — in the postures of lifelong, numbing labor.", "The founding manifesto of Realism. Destroyed in the Dresden bombing of 1945. Courbet showed the working class at life scale for the first time.", "male", "French"),
    ("Gustave Courbet: The Painter's Studio", "Gustave Courbet", 1855, "Oil on canvas", "Realism / French", ["allegorical","monumental","studio","realist","large scale"], ["painter","model","critics","friends","society","studio"], ["brown","warm","theatrical light","crowd"], "Musée d'Orsay, Paris", "A vast studio scene with Courbet painting a landscape model, flanked by his social world: workers, critics, intellectuals.", "A 'real allegory' — Courbet's term — of his position in society. At 6 meters wide, it is his most ambitious statement.", "male", "French"),
    ("Honoré Daumier: Third-Class Carriage", "Honoré Daumier", 1863, "Oil on canvas", "Realism / French", ["realist","social","urban","quiet","empathetic"], ["working class","railway","tired figures","mother","child","old woman"], ["dark","brown","grey","working class"], "Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York", "Three generations — an elderly woman, a young mother nursing, a sleeping child — ride third class in a crowded railway carriage.", "Daumier's rare oil paintings are even more powerful than his caricatures. This image of the urban poor riding third class is quietly devastating.", "male", "French"),
    ("Rosa Bonheur: The Horse Fair", "Rosa Bonheur", 1855, "Oil on canvas", "Realism / French", ["realist","equine","dynamic","large scale","energetic"], ["horses","riders","fair","movement","animal"], ["brown","cream","dust","golden light"], "Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York", "Dozens of horses wheel and rear at the Paris horse market, handlers struggling to control them in a panorama of animal energy.", "Bonheur was the most celebrated woman artist of the 19th century. She obtained a police permit to dress as a man to sketch at the horse fair.", "female", "French"),

    # ── SYMBOLISM & ART NOUVEAU ────────────────────────────────────────────
    ("Gustave Moreau: Salomé Dancing before Herod", "Gustave Moreau", 1876, "Oil on canvas", "Symbolism / French", ["symbolist","jeweled","ornate","mythological","sensuous"], ["Salomé","dance","Herod","jewels","exotic","biblical"], ["gold","dark","jewel tones","rich fabric"], "Hammer Museum, Los Angeles", "Salomé dances before the enthroned Herod in an impossibly jeweled interior, her gesture pointing toward the severed head of John the Baptist.", "The painting that made Huysmans's 'Against Nature' possible. Decadent Symbolism at its most ornate.", "male", "French"),
    ("Odilon Redon: The Cyclops", "Odilon Redon", 1914, "Oil on panel", "Symbolism / French", ["symbolist","dreamlike","colorful","mythological","tender"], ["cyclops","Polyphemus","Galatea","sleeping","nature"], ["pink","blue","green","yellow","flower colors"], "Kröller-Müller Museum, Netherlands", "A single giant eye rises from behind a hill to gaze tenderly at a sleeping nymph in a landscape of extraordinary floral color.", "One of Redon's most tender mythological images. His late work translated Symbolist darkness into radiant color.", "male", "French"),
    ("Fernand Khnopff: I Lock My Door upon Myself", "Fernand Khnopff", 1891, "Oil on canvas", "Symbolism / Belgian", ["symbolist","mysterious","enigmatic","withdrawal","female"], ["woman","lilies","statue","solitude","withdrawal"], ["red lilies","blue","cream","grey"], "Neue Pinakothek, Munich", "A woman with a hypnotic gaze sits surrounded by red lilies, with a bust of Hypnos (Sleep) and the brooding title inscribed on the frame.", "The paradigm of Symbolist solipsism. The title from Christina Rossetti. Khnopff's only sister was his obsessive model.", "male", "Belgian"),
    ("Jan Toorop: The Three Brides", "Jan Toorop", 1893, "Chalk drawing", "Symbolism / Dutch", ["symbolist","art nouveau","angular","ethereal","female"], ["three brides","good evil","hair flowing","bell","mystical"], ["cream","dark","flowing lines"], "Kröller-Müller Museum, Netherlands", "Three elongated women — the Earthly Bride, the Spiritual Bride, and the Satanic Bride — are connected by flowing hair and ropes of bells.", "A masterwork of Symbolist draftsmanship. Toorop's Javanese heritage (he grew up in Indonesia) visibly influences the elongated figural style.", "male", "Dutch"),
    ("Alphonse Mucha: Job (Cigarette Paper advertisement)", "Alphonse Mucha", 1896, "Color lithograph", "Art Nouveau / Czech", ["art nouveau","decorative","female","curvilinear","commercial"], ["woman","flowing hair","decorative border","poster","beauty"], ["cream","gold","green","brown","ornate border"], "Various collections", "A woman with flowing auburn hair fills a decorative Art Nouveau frame, her gaze dreamy and self-possessed.", "Mucha's poster style defined Art Nouveau graphics worldwide. The 'Mucha Style' became synonymous with the movement.", "male", "Czech"),

    # ── PHOTOGRAPHY AS ART ────────────────────────────────────────────────
    ("Alfred Stieglitz: The Steerage", "Alfred Stieglitz", 1907, "Photogravure", "Photography / Pictorialist", ["photograph","compositional","social","divide","geometric"], ["steerage passengers","first class","gangway","class divide","ship"], ["black and white","grey tones"], "Museum of Modern Art, MoMA", "First-class passengers on a gangway above; third-class passengers crammed below. The composition is formally perfect, the social division stark.", "Stieglitz called it the most important photograph he ever took. A social document and formal masterpiece that legitimized photography as fine art.", "male", "American"),
    ("Dorothea Lange: Migrant Mother", "Dorothea Lange", 1936, "Gelatin silver print", "Photography / Documentary", ["photograph","documentary","iconic","empathetic","social"], ["mother","children","poverty","Dust Bowl","Depression"], ["black and white","grey","intimate"], "Library of Congress, Washington D.C.", "Florence Owens Thompson with three children pressed against her. Her expression is exhausted, worried, and composed simultaneously.", "The defining image of the Great Depression. Lange took it in 10 minutes and sent it to the government. The family was not consulted for decades.", "female", "American"),
    ("Ansel Adams: Moonrise, Hernandez, New Mexico", "Ansel Adams", 1941, "Gelatin silver print", "Photography / American", ["photograph","landscape","luminous","monumental","american west"], ["moon","cemetery crosses","New Mexico","clouds","desert"], ["black and white","silver","luminous"], "Various collections", "A full moon rises over a tiny New Mexico village and cemetery as the last light of day illuminates the crosses.", "Adams recalled the exact exposure from memory after his light meter was inaccessible. His large-format landscapes defined the American wilderness ideal.", "male", "American"),

    # ── ABSTRACT & POST-WAR CONTINUED ─────────────────────────────────────
    ("Ad Reinhardt: Abstract Painting (Black)", "Ad Reinhardt", 1960, "Oil on canvas", "Abstract / Minimal", ["minimal","near-black","meditative","austere","square"], ["near-black","cross form","dark color","pure painting","silence"], ["black","near-black","very dark"], "Museum of Modern Art, MoMA", "A 60-inch square of near-black that, as the eyes adjust, reveals a barely visible cross of four slightly different dark shades.", "Reinhardt said this was 'the last painting anyone can paint'. Its near-invisible crosses can only be seen in perfect conditions — a meditation in paint.", "male", "American"),
    ("Agnes Martin: Untitled #5", "Agnes Martin", 1994, "Acrylic and graphite on canvas", "Minimal / Abstract", ["minimal","lines","quiet","meditative","horizontal"], ["horizontal lines","pale color field","quiet","grid","meditative"], ["pale cream","soft grey lines","white"], "Solomon R. Guggenheim Museum, New York", "A soft cream canvas with delicate penciled horizontal bands creating a vibrating field of quietude.", "Martin's grids and bands are not geometric in the hard-edge Minimalist sense but tender and hand-made. She called her work expressions of pure happiness.", "female", "Canadian-American"),
    ("Donald Judd: Untitled (Stack)", "Donald Judd", 1967, "Galvanized iron and amber Plexiglas", "Minimalism / American", ["minimal","industrial","stacked","serial","sculptural"], ["rectangular units","stack","wall","space","light through plexiglas"], ["galvanized silver","amber","regular intervals"], "Museum of Modern Art, MoMA", "Ten identical galvanized-iron units with amber Plexiglas bottoms project from the wall at equal intervals.", "Judd's 'specific objects' were neither painting nor sculpture. The stack creates rhythm, light play, and spatial precision. Minimalism at its purest.", "male", "American"),
    ("Dan Flavin: Monument for V. Tatlin", "Dan Flavin", 1964, "Fluorescent light fixtures", "Minimalism / American", ["minimal","light","industrial","monument","fluorescent"], ["fluorescent tubes","white light","tower form","industrial material"], ["white light","cool blue-white"], "Various collections", "A stack of white fluorescent light tubes arranged to evoke Tatlin's unrealized Tower of the Third International.", "Flavin used only commercially available fluorescent tubes. His tribute to the Soviet constructivist Tatlin is a cornerstone of American Minimalism.", "male", "American"),
    ("Yayoi Kusama: Accumulation No. 1", "Yayoi Kusama", 1962, "Sewn stuffed fabric on chair", "Neo-Dada / Pop / Japanese", ["repetition","obsessive","organic","soft sculpture","tactile"], ["chair","phallus forms","obsessive repetition","fabric","accumulation"], ["white","cream","fabric"], "Museum of Modern Art, MoMA", "An armchair covered with hundreds of soft phallic protrusions in white cotton fabric, sewn by hand.", "Kusama's obsessive repetition is her therapy — she has lived voluntarily in a psychiatric facility since 1977. Her work confronts trauma through accumulation.", "female", "Japanese"),
    ("Louise Bourgeois: Maman", "Louise Bourgeois", 1999, "Bronze, stainless steel, marble", "Contemporary / Sculptural", ["monumental","sculpture","bronze","maternal","terrifying"], ["spider","egg sac","steel legs","motherhood","protection"], ["dark bronze","steel grey"], "Various museums worldwide", "A colossal bronze spider — nearly 10 meters tall — stands on eight legs with a steel egg sac under its abdomen.", "Maman (Mother) was Bourgeois's tribute to her tapestry-weaver mother. The spider weaves and protects; it is also terrifying. Shown in the Tate Turbine Hall.", "female", "French-American"),
    ("Cindy Sherman: Untitled Film Still #21", "Cindy Sherman", 1978, "Gelatin silver print", "Conceptual / Photography", ["photograph","conceptual","female identity","role playing","noir"], ["woman","urban","anxiety","film noir","self-portrait"], ["black and white","urban grey","shadow"], "Museum of Modern Art, MoMA", "Sherman poses as an anonymous woman in a city street, looking anxiously over her shoulder in a scene from no particular film.", "Sherman's 'Untitled Film Stills' explore female stereotypes in cinema and culture. She plays every role herself. A cornerstone of feminist conceptual art.", "female", "American"),
    ("Kara Walker: A Subtlety (The Marvelous Sugar Baby)", "Kara Walker", 2014, "Sugar and polystyrene", "Contemporary / American", ["monumental","sculpture","race","historical","provocative"], ["sugar sphinx","slavery","plantation","woman","history"], ["white sugar","dark resin figures"], "Domino Sugar Factory, Brooklyn (demolished)", "A 12-meter sphinx made of pure white sugar in the form of a black woman, surrounded by small resin figures of sugar workers.", "Made inside the Domino Sugar Factory before its demolition. Walker's confrontation with slavery, sugar, and black female bodies is unflinching.", "female", "American"),
    ("Kerry James Marshall: Untitled (Painter)", "Kerry James Marshall", 2009, "Acrylic on PVC panel", "Contemporary / American", ["contemporary figurative","black figures","studio","painting","self-referential"], ["black painter","studio","canvas","art history","representation"], ["black figure","cream","bright colors","studio"], "Various collections", "A deeply black-skinned figure paints in a studio, surrounded by art historical references, claiming space in the Western painting tradition.", "Marshall's project is to insert black figures into the Western painting tradition at its most canonical. His works are among the most significant of the 21st century.", "male", "American"),

    # ── ITALIAN POST-WAR ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
    ("Lucio Fontana: Spatial Concept, Waiting", "Lucio Fontana", 1960, "Oil on canvas (slashed)", "Spatialism / Italian", ["conceptual","slashed","minimal","canvas","void"], ["slash","canvas","void","spatial","gesture"], ["monochrome canvas","the cut"], "Tate Modern, London", "A monochrome canvas slashed with a single, decisive cut that opens the surface to the void behind.", "Fontana literally opened painting to space. The slash is at once violent and surgical. It spawned Arte Povera and influenced Conceptual Art globally.", "male", "Italian"),
    ("Michelangelo Pistoletto: Venus of the Rags", "Michelangelo Pistoletto", 1967, "Painted marble, rags", "Arte Povera / Italian", ["arte povera","found objects","classical vs contemporary","pile","concept"], ["venus statue","pile of rags","high art","low material","contrast"], ["marble white","colorful rags"], "Various museums", "A classical Venus statue turns her back to a towering pile of colorful used rags.", "The juxtaposition of classical beauty and industrial waste is a founding gesture of Arte Povera. One of the most reproduced images of Italian post-war art.", "male", "Italian"),

    # ── SOUTH & SOUTHEAST ASIAN CONTINUED ────────────────────────────────
    ("Amrita Sher-Gil: Three Girls", "Amrita Sher-Gil", 1935, "Oil on canvas", "Indian Modernism", ["modernist","post-impressionist","indian","melancholic","figurative"], ["three girls","quiet","melancholic","Indian women","village"], ["ochre","dark skin","green","muted tones"], "National Gallery of Modern Art, New Delhi", "Three Indian women sit in meditative quiet, their gazes distant, dressed in simple saris.", "Sher-Gil merged Post-Impressionist technique with Indian subject matter. She died at 28; her work is the foundation of modern Indian painting.", "female", "Indian"),
    ("M.F. Husain: Horses", "M.F. Husain", 1980, "Oil on canvas", "Indian Modernism / Contemporary", ["expressionist","horses","dynamic","bold","modernist"], ["horses","movement","color","power","india"], ["bright color","earth","blue","dynamic brushwork"], "Various collections", "Powerful horses rendered in bold, gestural brushstrokes with an energy that recalls cave paintings.", "Husain was the most famous Indian artist of the 20th century — the 'Picasso of India'. His horse paintings combine Cubist energy with Indian mythology.", "male", "Indian"),
    ("Tyeb Mehta: Mahishasura", "Tyeb Mehta", 1996, "Oil on canvas", "Indian Modernism", ["expressionist","mythological","diagonal","bold","powerful"], ["demon","Mahishasura","goddess","battle","diagonal split"], ["red","dark blue","diagonal","dramatic"], "Christie's auction", "The demon Mahishasura and the goddess Durga collide along a diagonal split canvas in a battle of cosmic force.", "Mehta's diagonal split became his signature compositional device. Mahishasura sold for $1.5 million in 2002 — then a record for Indian art.", "male", "Indian"),
    ("Angkor Wat Apsara Reliefs", "Khmer sculptors", 1120, "Stone relief carving", "Khmer / Southeast Asian", ["relief","religious","repetitive","graceful","monumental"], ["apsaras","celestial dancers","multiple figures","stone","temple"], ["grey sandstone"], "Angkor Wat, Cambodia", "Rows of apsara (celestial dancer) figures carved in stone relief with individualized headdresses and jewelry.", "Over 1700 apsara figures decorate Angkor Wat, each subtly different. A supreme achievement of Khmer reliefs.", "unknown", "Cambodian"),
    ("Borobudur: The Life of the Buddha Reliefs", "Javanese sculptors", 800, "Stone relief carving", "Central Javanese Buddhist", ["relief","narrative","Buddhist","repetitive","monumental"], ["Buddha","life scenes","court","teaching","enlightenment"], ["grey volcanic stone"], "Borobudur, Central Java", "Continuous narrative reliefs running for 6 kilometers around the galleries of Borobudur depicting the life and previous lives of the Buddha.", "The largest Buddhist monument in the world. The 2,672 relief panels are the most extensive narrative stone carving program ever executed.", "unknown", "Indonesian"),

    # ── EAST AFRICAN & ETHIOPIAN ───────────────────────────────────────────
    ("Icon of St George Slaying the Dragon", "Ethiopian icon painters", 1800, "Tempera on gesso panel", "Ethiopian Christian Art", ["icon","religious","colorful","flat","devotional"], ["Saint George","dragon","horse","Christian icon","Ethiopia"], ["bright red","gold","blue","green","white"], "Various churches, Ethiopia", "Saint George in red armor drives his lance through the dragon while Princess Birutawit watches, in vivid flat tempera.", "Ethiopian icon painting has a continuous tradition from the 4th century. Its flat, brilliantly colored style is entirely its own — no western influence.", "unknown", "Ethiopian"),

    # ── OCEANIC & ABORIGINAL ──────────────────────────────────────────────
    ("Emily Kame Kngwarreye: Earth's Creation", "Emily Kame Kngwarreye", 1994, "Acrylic on canvas", "Contemporary Indigenous Australian", ["abstract","dot painting","land","spiritual","vast"], ["desert country","seeds","dreaming","country","dots"], ["yellow","orange","red","cream","brown"], "Private collection", "A 9-meter expanse of layered dots in yellow, orange, and cream suggests the cycles of desert life from seed to flower.", "Kngwarreye only began painting on canvas at the age of approximately 78. In 8 years she produced 3000 works. Earth's Creation is her masterpiece.", "female", "Australian Aboriginal"),
    ("Clifford Possum Tjapaltjarri: Warlugulong", "Clifford Possum Tjapaltjarri", 1977, "Acrylic on canvas", "Contemporary Indigenous Australian", ["dot painting","land map","dreaming","spiritual","ceremonial"], ["country map","ancestors","fire","site lines","dreaming tracks"], ["ochre","red","white","dark"], "Art Gallery of New South Wales", "A vast map of ancestral country showing Dreaming tracks, fire sites, and ceremonial ground in intricate dot painting.", "One of the first large-scale acrylic dot paintings. Maps the ancestral landscape of Warlugulong from above, fusing map and ceremony.", "male", "Australian Aboriginal"),
    ("Maori Meeting House Carving: Raharuhi Rukupo (Te Hau ki Tūranga)", "Raharuhi Rukupo and others", 1842, "Carved and painted wood", "Maori / Pacific", ["carved","spiral","figurative","ancestor","polychrome"], ["ancestor figure","scroll patterns","paua shell eyes","wharenui","tattoo"], ["red ochre","black","white","paua shell"], "Te Papa Tongarewa, Wellington", "Intricately carved ancestor figures with spiral tattoo patterns and gleaming paua-shell eyes line the walls and rafters of a meeting house.", "The most important surviving Maori meeting house. Rukupo carved it as a memorial to paramount chief Te Kani-a-Takirau. The figures are named ancestors.", "male", "Māori"),

    # ── ADDITIONAL WESTERN MODERN ─────────────────────────────────────────
    ("Egon Schiele: Self-Portrait with Physalis", "Egon Schiele", 1912, "Oil and gouache on panel", "Expressionism / Austrian", ["expressionist","self-portrait","raw","angular","psychological"], ["self-portrait","orange berry","gaunt","intense gaze","bare"], ["orange","flesh","dark background","cream"], "Leopold Museum, Vienna", "Schiele stares with burning intensity, a physalis (Chinese lantern) berry hanging above his gaunt angular neck.", "Schiele's self-portraits strip away all social mask. The physalis berry is the only touch of warmth in an otherwise unsparing confrontation.", "male", "Austrian"),
    ("Ernst Ludwig Kirchner: Marcella", "Ernst Ludwig Kirchner", 1910, "Oil on canvas", "Expressionism / German", ["expressionist","portrait","angular","psychological","bold color"], ["young woman","direct gaze","angular","bold background","model"], ["green","orange","red","angular brushwork"], "Moderna Museet, Stockholm", "A young woman sits with an intense gaze, her angular form built from bold strokes of orange, green, and red.", "One of Kirchner's finest portraits. The model Marcella was one of two girls who lived with the Brücke painters. The distorted color expresses her inner life.", "male", "German"),
    ("Juan Gris: Still Life with Checked Tablecloth", "Juan Gris", 1915, "Oil on canvas", "Synthetic Cubism / Spanish", ["cubist","synthetic cubism","collage elements","decorative","geometric"], ["guitar","bottle","tablecloth","newspaper","still life"], ["blue","cream","check pattern","brown","grey"], "Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York", "A table with guitar, bottle, and newspaper rendered in the decorative flat planes of Synthetic Cubism with a checked tablecloth.", "Gris's Synthetic Cubism is warmer and more decorative than Picasso or Braque. His still lifes are among the most beautiful objects of the movement.", "male", "Spanish"),
    ("Fernand Léger: The City", "Fernand Léger", 1919, "Oil on canvas", "Cubism / French", ["cubist","urban","mechanical","colorful","fragmented"], ["city","billboards","figures","stairs","machinery"], ["red","blue","cream","primary colors","geometric"], "Philadelphia Museum of Art", "A city of advertising posters, mechanical staircases, and fragmented figures in primary cubist color.", "Léger's vision of modern urban life as joyful machine. 'The City' is his most complex and celebrated large-scale Cubist composition.", "male", "French"),
    ("Giorgio de Chirico: The Enigma of an Autumn Afternoon", "Giorgio de Chirico", 1910, "Oil on canvas", "Metaphysical Art / Italian", ["metaphysical","uncanny","shadow","silence","strange perspective"], ["piazza","long shadows","arcade","solitary figure","silence"], ["ochre","dark shadow","blue sky","deserted"], "Private collection", "A deserted Italian piazza with long shadows and Romanesque arcades stretches into an unsettling afternoon silence.", "De Chirico's first 'metaphysical' painting, sparked by a hallucinatory vision in the Piazza Santa Croce. Directly inspired Surrealism.", "male", "Italian-Greek"),
    ("Giorgio de Chirico: The Disquieting Muses", "Giorgio de Chirico", 1916, "Oil on canvas", "Metaphysical Art / Italian", ["metaphysical","uncanny","mannequin","disquieting","symbolic"], ["mannequins","Ferrara tower","shadows","classical column","silence"], ["ochre","red tower","cream","long shadow"], "Private collection", "Two featureless mannequin figures inhabit a deserted Italian piazza in long afternoon shadow beneath a factory skyline.", "The painting that most directly inspired Surrealism. The mannequin figures without faces represent the uncanny in Freudian terms.", "male", "Italian-Greek"),
    ("Paul Nash: We Are Making a New World", "Paul Nash", 1918, "Oil on canvas", "British War Art", ["war art","expressionist","landscape","desolation","anti-war"], ["blasted trees","sunrise","mud","shell holes","desolation"], ["orange sunrise","black stumps","grey mud","blue"], "Imperial War Museum, London", "A desolate landscape of shattered tree stumps and mud under a brutal orange sunrise. The sarcastic title from a Lloyd George speech.", "Nash's WWI landscapes are among the most powerful anti-war images ever made. He wrote: 'I am no longer an artist — I am a messenger to the world.'", "male", "British"),
    ("Christopher Nevinson: Paths of Glory", "Christopher Nevinson", 1917, "Oil on canvas", "British War Art / Futurism", ["war art","futurist","diagonal","desolation","anti-war"], ["two dead soldiers","mud","barbed wire","shell holes","WWI"], ["grey mud","khaki","barbed wire"], "Imperial War Museum, London", "Two British soldiers lie face down dead in the mud. The British government censored it — Nevinson exhibited it with a strip of brown paper over the bodies.", "The most censored painting of WWI. Nevinson exhibited it anyway with 'censored' written on paper. Now a canonical image of war's futility.", "male", "British"),
    ("Eric Ravilious: Cuckmere Haven", "Eric Ravilious", 1939, "Watercolor", "British Modernism", ["watercolor","landscape","english","geometric","quiet"], ["English coast","chalk downs","river","geometric fields","sea"], ["grey blue","pale green","chalk white","sky"], "Tate Britain, London", "The Cuckmere meanders to the sea through chalk downland in Ravilious's characteristically quiet, geometric watercolor.", "Ravilious's English landscapes combine geometric modernism with pastoral tradition. He was killed as a war artist in 1942. Now among the most loved British artists.", "male", "British"),
    ("Ben Nicholson: White Relief", "Ben Nicholson", 1935, "Oil on carved board", "British Abstraction", ["abstract","relief","minimal","geometric","white"], ["carved circles","rectangles","shadows","white on white"], ["white","shadows","carved relief"], "Tate Modern, London", "Carved rectangles and circles of different depths in white-painted board create a play of light and shadow.", "Nicholson's white reliefs are among the purest abstract objects produced in Britain. Made during his time with Mondrian and Hepworth in the 1930s.", "male", "British"),
    ("Barbara Hepworth: Single Form", "Barbara Hepworth", 1962, "Bronze sculpture", "British Abstraction / Sculpture", ["sculptural","bronze","organic","void","memorial"], ["oval form","pierced hole","bronze","memorial","monument"], ["dark bronze","patina"], "United Nations, New York", "A tall oval bronze form with a single round hole cut through it, dedicated as a memorial to Dag Hammarskjöld.", "Hepworth's pierced forms distilled organic natural shapes to their essence. The UN commission was the largest sculpture she created.", "female", "British"),
    ("Henry Moore: Recumbent Figure", "Henry Moore", 1938, "Green Hornton stone", "British Modernism / Sculpture", ["sculptural","recumbent","monumental","landscape","organic"], ["reclining figure","landscape","stone","biomorphic","organic"], ["grey green stone","monumental"], "Tate Modern, London", "A massively simplified reclining human figure in green stone, its hollows and forms suggesting landscape as much as body.", "Moore's recumbent figures are simultaneously human and geological. Sited outdoors, they seem to grow from the earth itself.", "male", "British"),

    # ── PHOTOGRAPHY CONTINUED ─────────────────────────────────────────────
    ("Henri Cartier-Bresson: Behind the Gare Saint-Lazare", "Henri Cartier-Bresson", 1932, "Gelatin silver print", "Street Photography / French", ["photograph","decisive moment","reflection","leap","geometry"], ["leaping figure","puddle","reflection","iron fence","station"], ["black and white","reflection"], "Various collections", "A man leaps over a puddle behind the Paris train station, his reflection forming a perfect symmetry.", "The most celebrated example of Cartier-Bresson's 'decisive moment'. The perfect geometry — reflection, fence, poster, leap — will never recur.", "male", "French"),
    ("Robert Frank: The Americans (Political Rally)", "Robert Frank", 1956, "Gelatin silver print (from book)", "Photography / American", ["photograph","documentary","america","alienation","social"], ["political rally","crowd","flag","America","estrangement"], ["black and white","crowd grey"], "Various collections", "An American flag obscures most of the faces in a political crowd, leaving only eyes visible below the flag's edge.", "From Frank's epochal book 'The Americans' — the most influential photography book ever made. His outsider's eye for American alienation shocked the country.", "male", "Swiss-American"),
    ("Weegee: The Critic", "Weegee", 1943, "Gelatin silver print", "Street Photography / American", ["photograph","social contrast","documentary","flash","candid"], ["wealthy women","drunk woman","staring","contrast","class"], ["black and white","flash","night"], "International Center of Photography, New York", "Two fur-draped socialites arrive at an opening night while a disheveled drunk woman stares at them in undisguised contempt.", "Weegee staged or seized this shot; either way, it is the most withering image of class contrast in American photography.", "male", "American"),

    # ── KOREAN & SOUTHEAST ASIAN ──────────────────────────────────────────
    ("Joseon Dynasty: Moon Jar", "Unknown Joseon potter", 1700, "White porcelain", "Joseon / Korean", ["ceramic","white","simple","imperfect","meditative"], ["moon jar","white porcelain","round form","simple beauty"], ["white porcelain","slight grey"], "National Museum of Korea, Seoul", "A large white porcelain jar of near-perfect spherical form, slightly asymmetric, with a milky white glaze.", "The Moon Jar is the emblem of Joseon ceramic art. Its deliberate imperfection and serene whiteness embody Korean aesthetic philosophy of jeong (feeling).", "unknown", "Korean"),
    ("Kim Hongdo (Danwon): Genre Scenes — Wrestlers", "Kim Hongdo", 1780, "Ink and color on paper", "Joseon / Korean", ["genre","lively","ink","crowd scene","observation"], ["wrestlers","crowd watching","variety of expressions","genre scene"], ["ink brown","cream","pale washes"], "National Museum of Korea, Seoul", "Two wrestlers grapple in a ring while a crowd of spectators watches — each face and posture uniquely observed.", "From the famous album of genre scenes by Danwon. The most beloved genre painting in Korea, celebrated for its observational wit.", "male", "Korean"),
    ("Shin Saimdang: Embroidered Insects and Grasses", "Shin Saimdang", 1540, "Embroidery on silk", "Joseon / Korean", ["embroidery","botanical","detailed","graceful","female artist"], ["insects","grasses","flowers","botanical","silk"], ["green","cream","gold","detailed stitches"], "Various collections", "Butterflies, beetles, and flowering grasses rendered in meticulous embroidery stitches on silk.", "Shin Saimdang was the most celebrated female artist of the Joseon Dynasty and is depicted on the Korean 50,000 won note.", "female", "Korean"),
    ("Prambanan Temple Reliefs: Ramayana", "Central Javanese sculptors", 850, "Stone relief carving", "Central Javanese Hindu", ["relief","epic","detailed","narrative","Hindu"], ["Rama","Sita","Ravana","battle","gods"], ["grey stone","warm ochre"], "Prambanan Temple Compound, Java", "The inner balustrade of the Shiva temple carved with continuous relief panels showing the Ramayana epic.", "The Prambanan Ramayana reliefs are among the finest in the world — naturalistic, full of narrative detail, and carved in a unique Central Javanese style.", "unknown", "Indonesian"),

    # ── ADDITIONAL MASTERS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
    ("Sandro Botticelli: Portrait of a Youth", "Sandro Botticelli", 1483, "Tempera on panel", "Early Renaissance / Florentine", ["portrait","youth","melancholic","refined","linear"], ["young man","pensive gaze","dark background","hat"], ["dark","flesh","cream","red"], "National Gallery of Art, Washington", "A young man in a red cap stares with melancholy intelligence from a dark background.", "One of Botticelli's most psychologically probing portraits. The identity of the sitter is unknown.", "male", "Italian"),
    ("Tintoretto: The Finding of Moses", "Tintoretto", 1555, "Oil on canvas", "Venetian Renaissance / Mannerism", ["venetian","dramatic light","biblical","crowded","theatrical"], ["Moses","Pharaoh's daughter","servants","riverbank","discovery"], ["warm gold","dark","rich fabric","luminous"], "Prado Museum, Madrid", "The daughter of Pharaoh discovers the infant Moses in his basket on the bank of the Nile, surrounded by attendants.", "Tintoretto's dramatic light and theatrical arrangement of figures made him the heir of both Titian and Michelangelo in Venice.", "male", "Italian"),
    ("Peter Paul Rubens: The Garden of Love", "Peter Paul Rubens", 1634, "Oil on canvas", "Baroque / Flemish", ["baroque","sensuous","garden","joyful","dynamic"], ["garden","couples","cherubs","fountain","venus","love"], ["pink","cream","blue","green","gold"], "Museo del Prado, Madrid", "Elegantly dressed couples and cherubs make merry in a garden. Rubens painted his young second wife Helena Fourment as Venus.", "One of Rubens' most joyful late paintings, celebrating his second marriage. The garden of love tradition stretches from medieval to modern art.", "male", "Flemish"),
    ("Anthony van Dyck: King Charles I at the Hunt", "Anthony van Dyck", 1635, "Oil on canvas", "Baroque / Flemish", ["portrait","elegant","aristocratic","landscape","royal"], ["Charles I","horse","servants","landscape","casual pose"], ["silver grey","brown","gold","landscape green"], "Louvre Museum, Paris", "Charles I dismounts during a hunt, his casual pose radiating aristocratic ease against a dramatic landscape.", "The most influential royal portrait of the 17th century. Van Dyck's formula of the relaxed king became the template for royal portraiture.", "male", "Flemish"),
    ("Nicolas Poussin: The Rape of the Sabine Women", "Nicolas Poussin", 1634, "Oil on canvas", "French Classicism", ["classical","violent","architectural","dramatic","narrative"], ["sabine women","Roman soldiers","abduction","architectural","battle"], ["red","blue","cream","Roman architecture","dramatic"], "Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York", "Roman soldiers seize the Sabine women among the columns of an ancient forum. The figures are arranged like a classical frieze.", "Poussin's greatest dramatic composition. The freeze-like arrangement of gesturing figures would influence David's classical compositions.", "male", "French"),
    ("Élisabeth Vigée Le Brun: Self-Portrait with Daughter", "Élisabeth Vigée Le Brun", 1789, "Oil on canvas", "Neoclassicism / French", ["portrait","maternal","tender","classical","female artist"], ["mother","daughter","embrace","tender","intimate"], ["cream","warm skin","red sash","classical dress"], "Louvre Museum, Paris", "The artist embraces her daughter Julie in a tender, natural pose entirely unlike the stiff portraits of the era.", "Vigée Le Brun was the most celebrated female portraitist of the 18th century. This maternal self-portrait breaks all conventions of the genre.", "female", "French"),
    ("Rosa Bonheur: Portrait Study of a Bull", "Rosa Bonheur", 1848, "Oil on canvas", "Realism / French", ["realist","animal","detailed","powerful","large scale"], ["bull","animal study","muscular","naturalistic"], ["dark brown","cream","earth tones"], "Various collections", "A bull rendered with extraordinary anatomical precision, its muscular form filling the canvas.", "Bonheur studied at the Paris abattoirs (dressed as a man) to achieve this anatomical knowledge. Her animal paintings were unmatched in their era.", "female", "French"),
    ("Mary Cassatt: The Child's Bath", "Mary Cassatt", 1893, "Oil on canvas", "Impressionism / American", ["impressionistic","domestic","maternal","intimate","pattern"], ["mother","child","bath","basin","caring"], ["striped fabric","blue","skin","patterned carpet"], "Art Institute of Chicago", "A woman washes a child's feet in a basin. The flat patterned background of the carpet and pitcher, viewed from above, is radical.", "Cassatt's high vantage point and flat patterns reflect her deep study of Japanese prints. An intimate study of maternal care.", "female", "American"),
    ("Berthe Morisot: The Cradle", "Berthe Morisot", 1872, "Oil on canvas", "Impressionism / French", ["impressionistic","intimate","domestic","female","tender"], ["mother","cradle","gauze curtain","sleeping baby","watching"], ["white gauze","soft green","tender light"], "Musée d'Orsay, Paris", "A young mother looks at her sleeping baby through a gauze curtain with a soft, absorbed gaze.", "Morisot was the most important female Impressionist. The Cradle was the first Impressionist work to be accepted by the Salon (1873).", "female", "French"),
    ("Camille Claudel: The Waltz", "Camille Claudel", 1895, "Bronze sculpture", "Symbolism / French", ["sculpture","romantic","dynamic","twisting","sensuous"], ["couple","dance","waltz","twisting","embrace"], ["dark bronze"], "Musée Rodin, Paris", "Two figures — a man fully clothed, a woman draped in flowing fabric — twist together in a passionate waltz.", "Claudel was Rodin's assistant, student, and lover. This bronze captures erotic energy in twisting movement. She spent her last 30 years in an asylum.", "female", "French"),
    ("Louise Bourgeois: Cell (Eyes and Mirrors)", "Louise Bourgeois", 1989, "Steel, marble, mirrors, glass eyes", "Contemporary / Sculptural", ["installation","enclosure","mirrors","eyes","psychological"], ["cage","mirrors","eyes","self-reflection","trauma"], ["steel grey","glass","marble white"], "Hirshhorn Museum, Washington D.C.", "A cage-like steel enclosure contains marble spheres and glass eyes that multiply in mirrors, creating a claustrophobic hall of self-reflection.", "Bourgeois's 'Cells' are autobiographical psychological spaces. This one confronts the experience of being watched and watching oneself.", "female", "French-American"),
    ("Ana Mendieta: Silueta Series", "Ana Mendieta", 1976, "Earth/body work (photograph)", "Land Art / Performance", ["body","earth","site-specific","spiritual","female"], ["silhouette","earth","body","ritual","land"], ["earth brown","green","body form"], "Various collections (photographs)", "The outline of a female body pressed into earth, grass, and sand in the landscape, the body absent but its form present.", "Mendieta's Silueta series is a primal statement about female identity, the body, and landscape. She died under mysterious circumstances in 1985.", "female", "Cuban-American"),
    ("Shirin Neshat: Women of Allah (Speechless)", "Shirin Neshat", 1996, "RC print and ink", "Contemporary / Photography", ["photographic","text","veil","identity","political"], ["woman","calligraphy","gun","veil","identity"], ["black and white","ink text"], "Various collections", "A woman's veiled face covered in Farsi calligraphy holds a rifle at her cheek in a direct confrontation with the viewer.", "Neshat's series on Iranian women navigates feminism, Islam, and political resistance. The calligraphy is from Iranian women poets.", "female", "Iranian"),
    ("Wangechi Mutu: The Seated I", "Wangechi Mutu", 2019, "Bronze sculpture", "Contemporary African / Sculpture", ["sculpture","female figure","african","contemporary","bronze"], ["seated woman","bronze","stylized","power","presence"], ["dark bronze"], "Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York", "A monumental bronze figure of an African woman seated in a posture of dignified authority, placed in the museum's facade niches.", "The first woman and first person of color to have a permanent commission on the Metropolitan Museum's facade. A monumental assertion of African female presence.", "female", "Kenyan"),
    ("El Anatsui: Dusasa II", "El Anatsui", 2007, "Aluminum and copper wire", "Contemporary African / Sculpture", ["tapestry","aluminum","fluid","golden","monumental"], ["bottle caps","woven metal","cascade","gold","textile"], ["gold","copper","silver","bronze aluminum"], "Various museums", "Thousands of flattened aluminum liquor-bottle caps sewn with copper wire into a vast, fluid metallic tapestry that cascades like cloth.", "El Anatsui's metal tapestries address colonialism through the very materials of its commodity trade. Each work is uniquely installed.", "male", "Ghanaian"),
    ("Yinka Shonibare: Nelson's Ship in a Bottle", "Yinka Shonibare", 2010, "Fiberglass, Dutch wax fabric, steel", "Contemporary / British", ["conceptual","colonial","colorful","sculpture","irony"], ["ship","bottle","batik sails","colonial","irony"], ["colorful batik","glass bottle","white ship"], "National Maritime Museum, London (permanent)", "Nelson's flagship HMS Victory in a bottle, with all sails cut from Dutch wax batik fabric — the 'African' fabric actually made in the Netherlands.", "A postcolonial comment on British imperial mythology. The 'African' fabric in fact originated in the Netherlands and was sold to West Africa as a commercial product.", "male", "Nigerian-British"),
    ("Kehinde Wiley: Napoleon Leading the Army over the Alps", "Kehinde Wiley", 2005, "Oil on canvas", "Contemporary American / Figurative", ["contemporary","appropriation","black figure","classical","political"], ["black man on horse","Napoleon pose","floral background","power","race"], ["gold","ornate floral","dark horse","green","classical"], "Brooklyn Museum", "A young black man in contemporary urban clothing rides a rearing horse in the pose of David's Napoleon, against an ornate floral background.", "Wiley replaces white historical figures with black subjects in poses of power and glory. Later painted Barack Obama's official White House portrait.", "male", "American"),
    ("Jeff Koons: Balloon Dog (Orange)", "Jeff Koons", 1994, "Mirror-polished stainless steel", "Neo-Pop / American", ["sculpture","shiny","pop","childhood","reflective"], ["balloon dog","orange","reflective","stainless steel","childhood"], ["orange reflective steel"], "Various collections", "A monumental dog figure made of twisted balloons, rendered in highly polished orange stainless steel 3 meters tall.", "Sold for $58.4 million in 2013 — the record for a living artist at the time. Koons's balloon sculptures reflect the viewer and environment perfectly.", "male", "American"),
    ("Gerhard Richter: October 18, 1977", "Gerhard Richter", 1988, "Oil on canvas (15 paintings)", "Painting / German", ["blurred","grey","photographic","cycle","historical"], ["baader meinhof","death","blurred photograph","grey","historical"], ["grey","black","blurred whites"], "Museum of Modern Art, MoMA", "Fifteen blurred grey paintings derived from newspaper and police photographs of the RAF Baader-Meinhof Group's death in Stammheim Prison.", "Richter's most controversial work. Blurring as a formal device removes certainty from historical trauma. The cycle is now a monument of German post-war art.", "male", "German"),
    ("Gerhard Richter: 4096 Colours", "Gerhard Richter", 1974, "Oil on canvas", "Painting / German", ["geometric","color grid","systematic","rational","paint"], ["color squares","grid","systematic","pure painting"], ["all colors in systematic grid"], "Kunstsammlung NRW, Düsseldorf", "4096 small squares of color arranged in a grid generated by a systematic color-mixing algorithm.", "Richter's color charts address seriality, chance, and rational painting. Contrasting with his blurred photos, they define two poles of his output.", "male", "German"),
    ("Sigmar Polke: Watchtower", "Sigmar Polke", 1984, "Lacquer on fabric", "German Painting", ["conceptual","halftone","political","ironic","historical"], ["watchtower","dots","benday dots","surveillance","east germany"], ["grey halftone","dark","pattern fabric"], "Museum Ludwig, Cologne", "An East German watchtower rendered in magnified halftone dots on printed patterned fabric.", "Polke's benday-dot technique critiques both consumer culture (via Lichtenstein) and Cold War surveillance through the same formal irony.", "male", "German"),
    ("Anselm Kiefer: Sulamith", "Anselm Kiefer", 1983, "Oil, acrylic, emulsion, shellac, straw on canvas", "Neo-Expressionism / German", ["expressionist","dark","historical","monumental","material"], ["crypt","memorial hall","straw","burning","Nazi architecture"], ["dark brown","straw","black soot","gold"], "Saatchi Collection, London", "A massive Nazi memorial hall in perspective leads to a burning flame at the end, the Hebrew name 'Sulamith' inscribed above.", "Kiefer confronted German history directly when others avoided it. The material straw and shellac add physical decay to historical memory.", "male", "German"),
    ("Martin Kippenberger: Untitled (Lamp)", "Martin Kippenberger", 1988, "Oil on canvas", "Neo-Expressionism / German", ["expressionist","crude","ironic","figurative","dark humor"], ["lamp","shadow","room","clumsy paint","black"], ["dark","crude paint","black","yellow"], "Various collections", "A crudely painted floor lamp casting a shadow in a near-empty room — ugly, deliberate, and oddly poignant.", "Kippenberger's cultivated bad painting is the most sustained critique of German post-war culture. His lamp pictures have become touchstones of ironic figuration.", "male", "German"),
    ("Neo Rauch: Die Fuge", "Neo Rauch", 2007, "Oil on canvas", "Contemporary Figurative / German", ["figurative","dreamlike","socialist realism","strange","symbolic"], ["workers","surreal landscape","dream","DDR aesthetics","figures"], ["grey green","ochre","industrial blue","dreamlike"], "Museum der bildenden Künste, Leipzig", "Workers in socialist-realist garb perform obscure tasks in a dreamlike industrial landscape that quotes and distorts GDR mural painting.", "Rauch's paintings mine the visual language of socialist realism to create personal dream imagery. The Leipzig school he represents is now globally influential.", "male", "German"),
    ("Paula Rego: The Dance", "Paula Rego", 1988, "Acrylic on paper on canvas", "Contemporary Figurative / Portuguese-British", ["figurative","narrative","dark","ritualistic","female"], ["women dancing","moonlight","sea","ritual","stages of life"], ["dark green","blue","grey sea","moonlight"], "Tate Modern, London", "Groups of women at different life stages dance in moonlit stages by the sea — young, adult, and old — in a Portuguese coastal setting.", "Rego's most ambitious early large painting. The three groups of women circle through the stages of female life in an image of defiant solidarity.", "female", "Portuguese-British"),
    ("Marlene Dumas: The Widow", "Marlene Dumas", 1995, "Oil on canvas", "Contemporary Figurative / South African", ["figurative","raw","empathetic","faces","political"], ["veiled woman","mourning","grief","black cloth","loss"], ["black veil","flesh","grey","raw paint"], "Various collections", "A woman in a black mourning veil is rendered in raw, dripping paint that makes grief itself visible in the medium.", "Dumas's paintings of grief, desire, and political violence are among the most important figurative works of the late 20th century.", "female", "South African"),
    ("Ai Weiwei: Sunflower Seeds", "Ai Weiwei", 2010, "100 million porcelain seeds", "Contemporary Chinese / Installation", ["installation","porcelain","mass produced","political","labor"], ["porcelain seeds","factory labor","100 million","individual mass","china"], ["grey white porcelain","matte"], "Tate Modern, London (Turbine Hall)", "100 million individually hand-painted porcelain sunflower seeds filling the Tate Turbine Hall floor to a depth of 10 cm.", "Each seed was hand-crafted by 1600 artisans in Jingdezhen. About mass production, individual labor, and China's relationship to the world.", "male", "Chinese"),
    ("Zhang Xiaogang: Bloodline: Big Family No. 3", "Zhang Xiaogang", 1995, "Oil on canvas", "Contemporary Chinese", ["figurative","grey","family portrait","cultural revolution","memory"], ["family portrait","grey","Cultural Revolution","red thread","melancholic"], ["grey","flesh","muted color spots","red thread"], "Various collections", "Three grey family members in Cultural Revolution clothing are linked by a red thread — their expressions uniform, their individuality suppressed.", "Zhang's Bloodline series drew on Cultural Revolution family photographs. The grey palette and red thread embody collective trauma and suppressed individuality.", "male", "Chinese"),
    ("Cai Guo-Qiang: Sky Ladder", "Cai Guo-Qiang", 2015, "Gunpowder fireworks", "Contemporary Chinese / Performance", ["fireworks","ephemeral","performance","monumental","night sky"], ["ladder of fire","night sky","sea","ephemeral spectacle"], ["gold fire","black sky","sea reflections"], "Quanzhou, China (one night performance)", "A 500-meter firework ladder of fire ascended into the night sky above the sea off Quanzhou, lasting two and a half minutes.", "Cai's mother's wish, realized when she was 100 years old. The gunpowder ladder — connecting earth to cosmos — is his most personal work.", "male", "Chinese"),
    ("William Kentridge: Drawing for Sobriety (Kentridge studio films)", "William Kentridge", 1994, "Charcoal and pastel on paper (animated)", "Contemporary South African", ["animated drawing","charcoal","erasure","political","narrative"], ["charcoal drawing","erased marks","industrial south africa","memory","apartheid"], ["charcoal black","white paper","erasure traces"], "Various museums", "Drawings animated through the traces of erasure and re-drawing, creating films about industrial and political South Africa.", "Kentridge's process films — in which erasure is as visible as drawing — are among the most original art-forms invented in the late 20th century.", "male", "South African"),
    ("Zanele Muholi: Somnyama Ngonyama (Hail the Dark Lioness)", "Zanele Muholi", 2015, "Silver gelatin print", "Contemporary Photography / South African", ["photograph","self-portrait","black identity","adorned","political"], ["self-portrait","dark skin","adorned","direct gaze","ritual"], ["deep black","white highlights","stark contrast"], "Various collections", "Muholi photographs themselves with extreme contrast and elaborate adornment made from everyday objects — scouring pads, rubber gloves — as accessories.", "Muholi's series reclaims and celebrates black South African identity through a powerful confrontational self-portraiture practice.", "non-binary", "South African"),
    ("Katsushika Hokusai: A Fisherman's Wife (The Dream of the Fisherman's Wife)", "Katsushika Hokusai", 1814, "Woodblock print", "Edo Period / Ukiyo-e", ["erotic","shunga","fantastical","octopus","marine"], ["woman","octopus","sea","dream","erotic"], ["blue grey","cream","ink"], "Various collections", "A woman in an erotic encounter with two octopuses from Japanese legend — one of the most famous erotic images in Asian art history.", "Hokusai's shunga (erotic print) masterpiece. It has influenced artists from Rodin to modern graphic art. The merging of the human and marine is dreamlike.", "male", "Japanese"),
    ("Katsushika Hokusai: Self-Portrait as an Old Man", "Katsushika Hokusai", 1839, "Brush and ink on paper", "Edo Period / Japanese", ["self-portrait","aged","ink","humble","honest"], ["old man","bent posture","brush","aged face","walking stick"], ["ink brown","cream paper"], "Freer Gallery, Washington D.C.", "Hokusai depicts himself as a small, bent old man peering around a large screen, brush in hand.", "Hokusai produced this self-deprecating portrait at 80, still obsessively working. He reportedly said: 'From the age of six I had a passion for copying things.'", "male", "Japanese"),
